1
00:00:15,240 --> 00:00:16,610
(Did you enjoy today's date?)

2
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:19,680
(Seon Ho started to feel the clock ticking.)

3
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,250
(But do you want to keep talking to me?)

4
00:00:21,250 --> 00:00:23,480
(There's someone I'd like to get to know more.)

5
00:00:24,110 --> 00:00:27,350
(It seems Jong Eun can't return Ro Bin's feelings.)

6
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:30,420
(I kept thinking about Ro Bin.)

7
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:34,560
(Ryun Gi began showing his interest to Ro Bin.)

8
00:00:34,560 --> 00:00:36,060
(Let's have tea together. It's been a while.)

9
00:00:37,730 --> 00:00:40,400
(Do you think I didn't allocate my time to you?)

10
00:00:40,400 --> 00:00:42,200
(They both became sure of how each other felt.)

11
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:44,570
(I shouldn't question it. I should just follow my heart.)

12
00:00:44,870 --> 00:00:47,040
(I allocated 30 minutes to her because I was curious.)

13
00:00:47,810 --> 00:00:50,810
(Chaos brought by the 30 minutes he allocated without much thinking)

14
00:00:52,910 --> 00:00:53,940
(This is like watching a thriller.)

15
00:00:53,940 --> 00:00:57,110
(Will it be the start of a game-changing love triangle?)

16
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:02,220
(Love Against Time)

17
00:01:02,790 --> 00:01:03,990
(The night of Day 4)

18
00:01:03,990 --> 00:01:05,620
Do you want to play it as a warm-up?

19
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:07,460
- Sounds good.
- A warm-up?

20
00:01:07,460 --> 00:01:08,490
Should I try it?

21
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:11,160
(After their decisions in the Room of Time,)

22
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:13,030
(everyone is engrossed in playing a board game.)

23
00:01:13,030 --> 00:01:15,800
- Oh, my.
- My gosh.

24
00:01:22,540 --> 00:01:24,610
It said I didn't have a date tomorrow.

25
00:01:25,310 --> 00:01:26,440
I was a bit disappointed.

26
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:28,250
I was mostly disappointed.

27
00:01:32,450 --> 00:01:36,590
(Seo Ro Bin does not have a date tomorrow.)

28
00:01:38,160 --> 00:01:39,920
I sort of expected it.

29
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:42,930
But seeing the text message like that...

30
00:01:42,990 --> 00:01:46,130
made me think that things might not work out.

31
00:01:49,830 --> 00:01:53,270
(Kim Jong Eun does not have a date tomorrow.)

32
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:55,540
I realized that Min Young wasn't interested in me enough...

33
00:01:55,540 --> 00:01:57,170
to have a date with me.

34
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:05,220
(Kang Min Young does not have a date tomorrow.)

35
00:02:05,450 --> 00:02:07,350
I already knew I wouldn't get a date.

36
00:02:07,350 --> 00:02:09,120
I needed some time to think.

37
00:02:12,320 --> 00:02:15,830
(Kim Ryun Gi does not have a date tomorrow.)

38
00:02:16,030 --> 00:02:17,900
I didn't think much of it.

39
00:02:18,030 --> 00:02:19,660
I thought if I remained in the House...

40
00:02:19,660 --> 00:02:21,300
and got lucky, I might be able to...

41
00:02:21,300 --> 00:02:22,900
talk to Ro Bin.

42
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:27,040
(Their hearts...)

43
00:02:27,040 --> 00:02:30,670
(never quite seem to meet.)

44
00:02:30,740 --> 00:02:32,540
(DK)

45
00:02:32,540 --> 00:02:34,810
My gosh. Everyone is disappointed.

46
00:02:34,810 --> 00:02:36,250
Everyone has to stay in the House.

47
00:02:36,250 --> 00:02:38,250
Many of them allocated their 100 minutes only to 1 person.

48
00:02:38,250 --> 00:02:40,380
But they all didn't get matched for a date.

49
00:02:40,380 --> 00:02:41,690
- Right. Seriously.
- Seriously.

50
00:02:41,690 --> 00:02:42,920
Allocating 100 minutes won't work now.

51
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:44,960
If we drew out where everyone's feelings are headed,

52
00:02:44,960 --> 00:02:47,290
- it would be a total mess.
- It'd be a mess.

53
00:02:47,290 --> 00:02:48,790
How did it...

54
00:02:50,790 --> 00:02:52,060
I can't believe this.

55
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:54,730
When you take photos of flowers outside, they look so pretty.

56
00:02:54,730 --> 00:02:55,900
Really?

57
00:02:57,030 --> 00:03:01,710
(Jung Ye Ji has a date with Kim Seon Ho tomorrow.)

58
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:06,240
Yes. So this is...

59
00:03:06,240 --> 00:03:08,410
I doubt I was able to keep a straight face.

60
00:03:08,410 --> 00:03:10,910
I couldn't stop smiling in a subtle way.

61
00:03:10,910 --> 00:03:13,820
I probably couldn't stop that.

62
00:03:13,820 --> 00:03:17,050
I found myself liking him a bit more today.

63
00:03:23,330 --> 00:03:26,430
(Kim Na Young has a date with Kim Seon Ho tomorrow.)

64
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:27,870
(Bursting into laughter)

65
00:03:29,930 --> 00:03:31,070
What do I do?

66
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:34,000
(Na Young doesn't know what to do.)

67
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:35,210
What am I going to do?

68
00:03:35,870 --> 00:03:37,370
I'm so happy.

69
00:03:37,940 --> 00:03:39,180
I can't wait.

70
00:03:39,180 --> 00:03:41,680
(There's a big smile on Na Young's face.)

71
00:03:45,420 --> 00:03:47,680
(Seon Ho gets the text message too.)

72
00:03:48,690 --> 00:03:51,260
(Kim Seon Ho has a date with Jung Ye Ji...)

73
00:03:51,260 --> 00:03:53,790
(and Kim Na Young tomorrow.)

74
00:03:56,390 --> 00:03:57,630
I was quite surprised...

75
00:03:57,630 --> 00:04:00,200
to find out that Na Young allocated a lot of time to me.

76
00:04:00,200 --> 00:04:01,570
It surprised me.

77
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:05,040
It made me wonder if I focused only on one side of her.

78
00:04:05,100 --> 00:04:07,940
I thought that my curiosity would be satisfied tomorrow.

79
00:04:07,940 --> 00:04:10,010
That crossed my mind too.

80
00:04:11,680 --> 00:04:13,240
Gosh, hold on.

81
00:04:13,810 --> 00:04:15,180
My goodness.

82
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:17,550
Do you think Ye Ji figured it out?

83
00:04:17,550 --> 00:04:18,720
No way.

84
00:04:18,720 --> 00:04:20,220
There's no way she can figure it out.

85
00:04:20,220 --> 00:04:21,220
She's clueless.

86
00:04:21,220 --> 00:04:22,820
I bet she's not even thinking that's a possibility.

87
00:04:23,420 --> 00:04:25,120
Thinking about Ye Ji is driving me crazy.

88
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,990
- Why?
- Ye Ji...

89
00:04:26,990 --> 00:04:29,290
- She's going to find out now.
- She'll know they went on a date.

90
00:04:29,290 --> 00:04:30,930
- With Na Young.
- Yes.

91
00:04:30,930 --> 00:04:33,400
Ye Ji is going to have all kinds of feelings now.

92
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:35,070
There's going to be a storm.

93
00:04:35,270 --> 00:04:38,370
If there's even a tiny bit of misunderstanding...

94
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:40,170
Things are going to get messy.

95
00:04:42,170 --> 00:04:48,110
(A new atmosphere brought by an unexpected individual)

96
00:04:53,750 --> 00:04:59,660
(What changes will their day bring?)

97
00:05:02,460 --> 00:05:07,130
(Ye Ji and Na Young are getting ready for their date.)

98
00:05:08,900 --> 00:05:10,170
How is it going for you?

99
00:05:10,530 --> 00:05:11,570
- Me?
- Yes.

100
00:05:11,570 --> 00:05:13,440
(Na Young's question breaks the silence.)

101
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:17,940
I think I'm finding my direction gradually.

102
00:05:21,810 --> 00:05:24,820
Actually, when I looked at you and Seon Ho,

103
00:05:24,820 --> 00:05:26,780
I wondered...

104
00:05:26,780 --> 00:05:28,420
if you guys were only interested in each other.

105
00:05:28,520 --> 00:05:29,890
- I see.
- So...

106
00:05:29,890 --> 00:05:31,560
how should I put it?

107
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:33,220
Anyway,

108
00:05:33,490 --> 00:05:36,330
I never had a chance to talk to Seon Ho. Not even once.

109
00:05:36,330 --> 00:05:38,200
I wanted to talk to him at least once.

110
00:05:38,760 --> 00:05:40,800
- So I suggested that.
- I see.

111
00:05:45,370 --> 00:05:49,370
(An awkward silence falls between them.)

112
00:05:50,370 --> 00:05:53,340
(On the other hand, Seon Ho is done getting ready for the date.)

113
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:06,460
(Ye Ji and Na Young are in the room together.)

114
00:06:12,230 --> 00:06:13,460
(Stopping)

115
00:06:14,330 --> 00:06:18,200
(Na Young and Seon Ho met in front of the door.)

116
00:06:19,070 --> 00:06:20,240
(Seon Ho: Ye Ji.)

117
00:06:21,100 --> 00:06:22,210
Ye Ji.

118
00:06:22,570 --> 00:06:23,610
Ye Ji.

119
00:06:25,010 --> 00:06:26,480
- My goodness.
- Gosh.

120
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:28,310
Hold on. I can't watch this.

121
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:30,650
- I can't watch this, Ye Na.
- Me neither.

122
00:06:30,650 --> 00:06:32,050
I can't watch it.

123
00:06:32,520 --> 00:06:33,980
Na Young probably thought...

124
00:06:33,980 --> 00:06:35,590
- he came to find her.
- Right.

125
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:37,290
But he's asking for Ye Ji.

126
00:06:38,260 --> 00:06:39,890
This love triangle is crazy.

127
00:06:39,890 --> 00:06:41,120
Seon Ho.

128
00:06:41,120 --> 00:06:43,030
- It's making me feel uneasy.
- I can't watch this. Seriously.

129
00:06:44,560 --> 00:06:46,060
(Seon Ho: Ye Ji.)

130
00:06:46,060 --> 00:06:47,660
(Na Young: Ye Ji.)

131
00:06:48,230 --> 00:06:49,230
Ye Ji.

132
00:06:49,230 --> 00:06:51,800
(Na Young calls Ye Ji when Seon Ho looks for Ye Ji.)

133
00:06:52,670 --> 00:06:53,800
Now?

134
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:55,110
I see. Wait.

135
00:07:01,780 --> 00:07:02,980
(Glancing over)

136
00:07:08,750 --> 00:07:12,960
(Na Young can't stop feeling conscious of Ye Ji.)

137
00:07:15,090 --> 00:07:18,660
(She leaves the room on purpose.)

138
00:07:24,270 --> 00:07:28,540
(Ye Ji heads out for her date with Seon Ho before Na Young.)

139
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,180
Where did he go?

140
00:07:38,580 --> 00:07:39,880
- Ye Ji.
- Yes?

141
00:07:39,880 --> 00:07:41,350
Let's go out together.

142
00:07:46,320 --> 00:07:50,630
(Seon Ho and Ye Ji's third date has begun.)

143
00:07:52,960 --> 00:07:54,530
It's windy?

144
00:07:54,530 --> 00:07:56,230
Yes, that's what the forecast said.

145
00:07:57,630 --> 00:07:58,970
You don't like windy days, do you?

146
00:07:59,270 --> 00:08:00,340
No.

147
00:08:00,900 --> 00:08:02,240
Put on your seatbelt.

148
00:08:03,270 --> 00:08:04,780
(They're much more comfortable around each other...)

149
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:06,280
(after their talk the night before.)

150
00:08:07,240 --> 00:08:09,010
(Seon Ho puts in the destination.)

151
00:08:09,010 --> 00:08:10,010
What?

152
00:08:11,310 --> 00:08:12,650
(Surprised)

153
00:08:15,790 --> 00:08:16,790
Let's do this.

154
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:18,160
(Seon Ho surprises her with the date he planned.)

155
00:08:18,360 --> 00:08:19,690
We're going to the beach?

156
00:08:21,020 --> 00:08:22,760
- Are you sure? It's a long drive.
- Yes.

157
00:08:22,760 --> 00:08:24,130
I'll be fine. Let's get going now.

158
00:08:24,460 --> 00:08:25,700
(Excited)

159
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:27,700
Isn't taking a girl to the beach making it official?

160
00:08:27,700 --> 00:08:29,530
It's almost official.

161
00:08:29,830 --> 00:08:33,240
Actually, as for Seon Ho and Ye Ji,

162
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:35,340
they started at 50 minutes.

163
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:38,280
Then they increased their time to 70 and 80 minutes.

164
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,910
- So that might be different now.
- Yes.

165
00:08:39,910 --> 00:08:40,980
Right.

166
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:43,380
Can you drive if I get too tired?

167
00:08:44,820 --> 00:08:46,520
- Do you trust me?
- No.

168
00:08:48,950 --> 00:08:55,790
(Their date begins with a wave of exciting energy.)

169
00:08:59,930 --> 00:09:01,430
Gosh, this is crazy. Seriously.

170
00:09:01,430 --> 00:09:02,600
We're going to the beach?

171
00:09:03,100 --> 00:09:05,400
I think it's this way. Let me turn here.

172
00:09:06,270 --> 00:09:07,770
I really wanted to go to the beach.

173
00:09:07,870 --> 00:09:08,870
- Really?
- Yes.

174
00:09:08,870 --> 00:09:09,870
That's good to hear.

175
00:09:10,440 --> 00:09:11,880
- I love it.
- Yes.

176
00:09:12,010 --> 00:09:13,080
- You too, right?
- Yes.

177
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,810
- I also like the beach.
- Yes.

178
00:09:17,480 --> 00:09:21,720
So you live in Gwangju. Do you get to see the beach often?

179
00:09:22,190 --> 00:09:23,820
It's not that far.

180
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,790
I often went to Yeosu and Mokpo.

181
00:09:27,790 --> 00:09:29,560
"I often went to Yeosu and Mokpo."

182
00:09:29,660 --> 00:09:30,790
(Laughing)

183
00:09:32,900 --> 00:09:34,700
I've never been to Yeosu.

184
00:09:34,700 --> 00:09:36,000
- Never?
- Never.

185
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:37,070
I'd love to visit.

186
00:09:37,070 --> 00:09:38,200
- Really?
- Yes.

187
00:09:39,100 --> 00:09:40,340
Should we pencil that in for later?

188
00:09:42,340 --> 00:09:44,210
(Surprised)

189
00:09:44,980 --> 00:09:47,640
(Seon Ho's flirting catches her off guard.)

190
00:09:48,310 --> 00:09:50,110
(She doesn't know how to respond.)

191
00:09:50,110 --> 00:09:51,150
I'm just saying.

192
00:09:53,180 --> 00:09:55,320
How long does it take to Busan from Gwangju?

193
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:58,660
It takes about the same time as going to Seoul.

194
00:10:00,060 --> 00:10:01,960
As far as I know,

195
00:10:01,960 --> 00:10:03,890
the transit options between Busan and Gwangju...

196
00:10:04,730 --> 00:10:07,230
- aren't great.
- I see.

197
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:09,800
I don't know what will happen with us in the future.

198
00:10:10,200 --> 00:10:13,740
If I were to go to Busan, I think I would probably drive.

199
00:10:14,940 --> 00:10:16,240
Busan is a great city.

200
00:10:17,110 --> 00:10:18,780
(Smiling)

201
00:10:19,510 --> 00:10:22,610
There was a time when I wanted to live in Busan.

202
00:10:23,310 --> 00:10:24,880
- In Busan?
- Yes. I visited Busan before.

203
00:10:24,880 --> 00:10:26,420
I really liked it there.

204
00:10:26,580 --> 00:10:28,690
- I see.
- The beach was so accessible.

205
00:10:29,590 --> 00:10:32,260
- I really liked my time in Busan.
- Right.

206
00:10:37,090 --> 00:10:40,560
How did it go for you yesterday in the Room of Time?

207
00:10:42,800 --> 00:10:44,700
It was tough. Well,

208
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:47,200
I didn't know how you felt.

209
00:10:49,610 --> 00:10:53,340
I told you two days ago that I allocated my time to you.

210
00:10:53,680 --> 00:10:54,740
But...

211
00:10:55,180 --> 00:10:57,080
we didn't get matched for a date.

212
00:10:58,620 --> 00:11:01,220
So I thought that...

213
00:11:01,820 --> 00:11:03,990
you weren't interested in me enough to get matched for a date.

214
00:11:04,390 --> 00:11:05,860
That crossed my mind.

215
00:11:06,560 --> 00:11:08,690
I just naturally assumed that...

216
00:11:09,160 --> 00:11:10,790
you'd go out on a date with someone else.

217
00:11:10,790 --> 00:11:12,660
So did you skip allocating time to me two days ago?

218
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:16,800
I did. But I think I made the wrong decision then.

219
00:11:16,800 --> 00:11:18,970
(But I think I made the wrong decision then.)

220
00:11:22,010 --> 00:11:23,110
Things are going well.

221
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:25,380
- Nice.
- Yes.

222
00:11:25,380 --> 00:11:26,680
Everything seems to be going well.

223
00:11:26,780 --> 00:11:28,480
Ye Na, you're in a good mood.

224
00:11:28,480 --> 00:11:30,480
I'm so happy right now.

225
00:11:31,650 --> 00:11:33,320
- It's peaceful, isn't it?
- This is the best.

226
00:11:35,850 --> 00:11:37,950
So when I thought about it,

227
00:11:38,660 --> 00:11:41,290
I should have divided my time...

228
00:11:41,290 --> 00:11:43,030
based on the level of my interest.

229
00:11:43,030 --> 00:11:44,030
I see.

230
00:11:44,730 --> 00:11:46,400
But the depth is different...

231
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:49,270
- between just being curious...
- Right.

232
00:11:49,670 --> 00:11:51,100
- and actually being interested.
- Right.

233
00:11:52,770 --> 00:11:55,310
Anyway, it was easier to make my decision yesterday...

234
00:11:55,310 --> 00:11:56,570
because I followed my heart.

235
00:11:58,510 --> 00:12:00,380
Same here. Yesterday was the easiest.

236
00:12:02,980 --> 00:12:04,150
- Is that so?
- Yes.

237
00:12:04,150 --> 00:12:06,380
(They followed their heart yesterday and allocated time to each other.)

238
00:12:07,620 --> 00:12:09,620
Do you prefer going to the beach at night...

239
00:12:09,620 --> 00:12:11,050
or during the day?

240
00:12:12,660 --> 00:12:15,030
- It's a tough choice.
- Okay.

241
00:12:15,160 --> 00:12:17,360
I like going to the beach at night in summer.

242
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,900
- The night beach in summer?
- Yes.

243
00:12:20,930 --> 00:12:22,500
- Can you see the beach?
- Gosh.

244
00:12:24,100 --> 00:12:26,940
(The cool summer ocean unfolds before their eyes.)

245
00:12:26,940 --> 00:12:27,970
It's beautiful.

246
00:12:29,110 --> 00:12:31,840
- Today's weather is amazing.
- Yes. It is.

247
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,880
This is so unreal.

248
00:12:34,880 --> 00:12:36,950
- I can't believe we're here.
- It's like a dreamy day.

249
00:12:40,220 --> 00:12:43,590
(Yeongjong Island)

250
00:12:47,020 --> 00:12:50,730
(The two of them arrive at a restaurant for grilled clams.)

251
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:53,830
Gosh, this is amazing.

252
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:55,370
I love it here.

253
00:12:58,230 --> 00:13:00,700
(The sky is clear without a single cloud.)

254
00:13:01,400 --> 00:13:04,110
Oh, my. No way. The atmosphere here is great.

255
00:13:04,710 --> 00:13:06,280
I need to take a picture.

256
00:13:08,140 --> 00:13:09,350
Do you want me to take a picture of you?

257
00:13:10,310 --> 00:13:11,550
Let me take a picture of you.

258
00:13:11,750 --> 00:13:12,850
- Of me?
- Yes.

259
00:13:14,250 --> 00:13:16,390
(Smiling)

260
00:13:17,790 --> 00:13:19,160
(Giggling)

261
00:13:21,760 --> 00:13:23,330
- This came out really well.
- My gosh.

262
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,200
What a pretty picture.

263
00:13:33,440 --> 00:13:34,470
It looks good.

264
00:13:34,470 --> 00:13:36,340
- Right. It already smells great.
- Yes.

265
00:13:37,040 --> 00:13:38,610
- This looks so good.
- Yes.

266
00:13:38,610 --> 00:13:39,910
- Enjoy.
- Let's do the clam-clink.

267
00:13:42,350 --> 00:13:43,380
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

268
00:13:44,450 --> 00:13:45,450
(Popping it in)

269
00:13:47,580 --> 00:13:48,650
Is it good?

270
00:13:51,490 --> 00:13:52,590
(Spotting)

271
00:13:52,590 --> 00:13:54,090
(Look at this.)

272
00:13:57,560 --> 00:13:59,200
It's moving. Did you see that?

273
00:13:59,200 --> 00:14:00,230
What?

274
00:14:00,230 --> 00:14:01,400
(Surprised)

275
00:14:01,830 --> 00:14:03,030
(Opening)

276
00:14:05,640 --> 00:14:06,900
- Do you know "SpongeBob?" - What's that?

277
00:14:08,770 --> 00:14:10,070
Of course.

278
00:14:12,180 --> 00:14:15,310
(Just the sight of the clam makes them smile.)

279
00:14:18,850 --> 00:14:20,220
(Pointing)

280
00:14:20,220 --> 00:14:21,320
They're flying away.

281
00:14:23,820 --> 00:14:25,420
Of course, birds fly away.

282
00:14:25,890 --> 00:14:27,320
"Of course, birds fly away."

283
00:14:27,320 --> 00:14:28,390
(A thinking type)

284
00:14:29,290 --> 00:14:30,960
Watching the birds fly away makes them happy.

285
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,760
Watching the clam move excites them.

286
00:14:32,760 --> 00:14:33,800
Right.

287
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:35,200
Coming to the beach was the right call.

288
00:14:36,030 --> 00:14:37,570
- Right.
- It's so peaceful.

289
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:41,600
(They look up at the sky together.)

290
00:14:42,410 --> 00:14:43,510
What's that?

291
00:14:44,870 --> 00:14:46,110
Maybe, it's an airplane.

292
00:14:46,380 --> 00:14:48,010
(Smiling)

293
00:14:53,450 --> 00:14:55,290
By the way...

294
00:14:56,450 --> 00:14:57,490
Yes?

295
00:14:58,020 --> 00:14:59,290
do I give off big sister vibes?

296
00:15:01,220 --> 00:15:02,660
Well, no.

297
00:15:03,690 --> 00:15:04,930
Wait, did that offend you?

298
00:15:04,990 --> 00:15:06,930
(Blushing)

299
00:15:08,000 --> 00:15:10,700
That's not how I see you when I'm with you.

300
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:13,670
You might see me as a younger brother.

301
00:15:14,800 --> 00:15:16,740
Well, that's up to you.

302
00:15:17,570 --> 00:15:18,980
I don't see you like that.

303
00:15:19,340 --> 00:15:21,040
- When we first met, - Yes.

304
00:15:21,440 --> 00:15:23,680
you did look very young. Just appearance-wise.

305
00:15:23,680 --> 00:15:24,680
I see.

306
00:15:24,810 --> 00:15:27,350
You had this look on your face.

307
00:15:27,350 --> 00:15:28,590
What's that? You keep saying that.

308
00:15:30,590 --> 00:15:32,120
Well, I thought you were...

309
00:15:32,120 --> 00:15:34,290
I mean, I expected you to be much younger.

310
00:15:35,260 --> 00:15:37,960
- But we're only one year apart.
- Yes, that's right.

311
00:15:38,930 --> 00:15:40,100
So that concerns me a bit.

312
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:43,570
I didn't want to come across as a younger guy.

313
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:45,070
That worried me a bit.

314
00:15:45,470 --> 00:15:48,770
And I'm the same age as your younger brother.

315
00:15:49,170 --> 00:15:52,540
So I thought that you were bound to see me as one.

316
00:15:52,810 --> 00:15:54,080
I was worried about that.

317
00:15:54,080 --> 00:15:55,650
- I see. Really?
- Yes.

318
00:15:56,180 --> 00:15:57,180
But...

319
00:15:57,680 --> 00:15:59,120
in the end, it's the person that matters.

320
00:15:59,120 --> 00:16:00,950
(It's the person that matters.)

321
00:16:02,350 --> 00:16:04,120
(Smiling)

322
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:05,960
- This one looked cooked.
- Yes.

323
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:07,820
Thank you.

324
00:16:09,060 --> 00:16:10,160
This one is cooked too.

325
00:16:10,930 --> 00:16:12,000
Thank you.

326
00:16:18,500 --> 00:16:19,570
Gosh, I'm so happy.

327
00:16:23,110 --> 00:16:25,780
Actually, up until yesterday... No, up until two days ago,

328
00:16:25,980 --> 00:16:28,340
I felt conflicted and had a lot on my mind.

329
00:16:29,350 --> 00:16:32,050
But I decided to stop thinking.

330
00:16:34,780 --> 00:16:37,650
I just decided to follow my heart.

331
00:16:39,090 --> 00:16:40,990
I'm not going to overthink it...

332
00:16:40,990 --> 00:16:43,690
or try to decode what I'm feeling.

333
00:16:44,630 --> 00:16:45,830
I'll just keep it simple.

334
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:48,630
"I was happy when I was with her."

335
00:16:49,400 --> 00:16:51,370
I decided to focus on that.

336
00:16:54,700 --> 00:16:57,070
I also felt like I was running out of time.

337
00:16:58,010 --> 00:16:59,380
I was worried that...

338
00:16:59,380 --> 00:17:01,410
nothing would happen at this rate.

339
00:17:02,710 --> 00:17:03,810
Well,

340
00:17:04,380 --> 00:17:05,850
the others must have had...

341
00:17:05,850 --> 00:17:07,820
enough chances just like I did.

342
00:17:08,590 --> 00:17:10,350
I felt like if I hesitated,

343
00:17:13,890 --> 00:17:15,990
nothing would ever become clear...

344
00:17:17,530 --> 00:17:18,760
between us.

345
00:17:19,730 --> 00:17:20,930
That's what I was thinking mostly.

346
00:17:20,930 --> 00:17:23,200
(Seon Ho opens up to her for the first time.)

347
00:17:23,630 --> 00:17:26,770
Seon Ho is expressing himself a lot today.

348
00:17:26,770 --> 00:17:29,210
Seriously. He suddenly became a different man.

349
00:17:29,740 --> 00:17:30,810
I can't get used to this.

350
00:17:30,810 --> 00:17:33,340
- He's different every day.
- He did change a lot.

351
00:17:33,340 --> 00:17:35,210
- He's totally a different person.
- Yes.

352
00:17:35,710 --> 00:17:37,480
They look like a real couple to me now.

353
00:17:40,120 --> 00:17:41,280
That's where I stand now.

354
00:17:51,060 --> 00:17:53,230
What do you look for in men?

355
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:57,430
I'm sure there are qualities you look for in men.

356
00:17:57,430 --> 00:17:59,670
- Or you must have an ideal type.
- I...

357
00:18:01,100 --> 00:18:02,810
I want someone...

358
00:18:02,810 --> 00:18:05,410
who's always sweet and sensitive when we talk.

359
00:18:05,410 --> 00:18:06,940
I want someone...

360
00:18:07,310 --> 00:18:08,950
who's capable of having fun...

361
00:18:08,950 --> 00:18:10,580
and engaging in a serious conversation like this.

362
00:18:11,510 --> 00:18:12,950
I'd love to meet someone like that.

363
00:18:12,950 --> 00:18:15,890
That's what I've been mostly thinking about my ideal type.

364
00:18:21,120 --> 00:18:22,830
Do you think you found someone like that here?

365
00:18:22,830 --> 00:18:25,300
(Do you think you found someone like that here?)

366
00:18:31,500 --> 00:18:33,770
My ideal type, personality-wise?

367
00:18:34,170 --> 00:18:35,240
Yes, sure.

368
00:18:36,970 --> 00:18:38,210
I guess you can say that. Yes.

369
00:18:39,740 --> 00:18:40,780
(Glancing up)

370
00:18:42,450 --> 00:18:45,050
Yes, I think I found someone close.

371
00:18:45,050 --> 00:18:48,250
(I think I found someone close to my ideal type.)

372
00:18:51,250 --> 00:18:52,390
What about you, Seon Ho?

373
00:18:57,090 --> 00:18:58,660
I think I did too.

374
00:19:06,670 --> 00:19:08,640
They're so cute!

375
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:10,610
They're so lovable and adorable.

376
00:19:10,810 --> 00:19:12,410
- My gosh.
- They must really like each other.

377
00:19:12,410 --> 00:19:14,740
Oh, my. Wait. They like each other way too much.

378
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:16,510
Gosh, Seon Ho is the man.

379
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:17,510
(Getting the butterflies)

380
00:19:19,120 --> 00:19:20,120
(Giving him food)

381
00:19:22,190 --> 00:19:23,990
You should eat some too.

382
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,890
(Blushing)

383
00:19:27,320 --> 00:19:29,230
I'm eating a lot.

384
00:19:29,230 --> 00:19:30,230
I see.

385
00:19:33,430 --> 00:19:35,060
Oh, right. Thank you for this.

386
00:19:38,100 --> 00:19:39,100
My gosh.

387
00:19:39,100 --> 00:19:40,740
(Seon Ho put the adhesive bandage on her finger the day before.)

388
00:19:41,770 --> 00:19:43,240
(The night before)

389
00:19:43,810 --> 00:19:45,780
(I'll do it.)

390
00:19:45,780 --> 00:19:48,280
(I'll do it. Stay still.)

391
00:19:49,650 --> 00:19:53,620
(He treated her finger when Ye Ji hurt it.)

392
00:19:59,520 --> 00:20:00,520
My gosh.

393
00:20:02,730 --> 00:20:03,930
Why does it look so funny?

394
00:20:05,500 --> 00:20:06,860
(Gently grabbing)

395
00:20:07,030 --> 00:20:08,160
Are you okay now?

396
00:20:08,260 --> 00:20:10,070
- Do you have the nail clipper?
- Yes.

397
00:20:10,070 --> 00:20:11,070
Yes.

398
00:20:11,670 --> 00:20:13,040
I didn't do anything to it yet.

399
00:20:13,040 --> 00:20:15,340
It didn't come off yet.

400
00:20:20,140 --> 00:20:21,740
Do you like summer or winter?

401
00:20:22,450 --> 00:20:23,480
I think...

402
00:20:24,010 --> 00:20:27,180
I still like winter.

403
00:20:28,380 --> 00:20:30,120
- You're a summer person, right?
- No.

404
00:20:30,390 --> 00:20:31,420
- Then winter?
- Yes.

405
00:20:31,420 --> 00:20:33,020
- Really?
- I don't like summer.

406
00:20:33,020 --> 00:20:34,560
I sweat easily.

407
00:20:34,790 --> 00:20:37,230
I can't stand that sticky feeling.

408
00:20:38,860 --> 00:20:42,060
My body gets cold quite easily.

409
00:20:42,060 --> 00:20:43,070
Okay.

410
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:45,470
So my hands and feet are very often cold.

411
00:20:45,470 --> 00:20:46,470
Really?

412
00:20:47,500 --> 00:20:49,270
- I...
- When I lie down to go to sleep,

413
00:20:49,270 --> 00:20:51,270
- my feet...
- Are they cold?

414
00:20:51,270 --> 00:20:52,280
They're like ice.

415
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:57,750
I'm the opposite. I have a lot of body heat.

416
00:21:03,790 --> 00:21:07,060
I have the warmest hands.

417
00:21:07,060 --> 00:21:08,760
- They don't get sweaty. Yes.
- Really?

418
00:21:09,460 --> 00:21:11,330
My feet are cold even in summer.

419
00:21:11,660 --> 00:21:12,700
- Really?
- Yes.

420
00:21:12,700 --> 00:21:14,460
I need something to cool me down.

421
00:21:16,170 --> 00:21:18,230
- My gosh. Come on now!
- Goodness.

422
00:21:18,670 --> 00:21:19,940
Who is this guy?

423
00:21:20,040 --> 00:21:21,370
He's such a fox.

424
00:21:21,470 --> 00:21:23,670
What are we watching now? "Elemental?"

425
00:21:24,070 --> 00:21:25,540
"Elemental?"

426
00:21:25,540 --> 00:21:26,840
(Anyone's first time using poor circulation to flirt...)

427
00:21:26,840 --> 00:21:28,110
(on a dating show)

428
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:30,580
My gosh. Now that they confirmed that they like each other,

429
00:21:30,580 --> 00:21:33,020
- he's super expressive.
- Right.

430
00:21:33,020 --> 00:21:34,450
He's just going for it.

431
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:36,150
Right. Watching them interact makes me think...

432
00:21:36,150 --> 00:21:37,490
they're practically a couple.

433
00:21:37,490 --> 00:21:39,020
Seriously. It's official.

434
00:21:41,190 --> 00:21:44,190
(I need something to cool me down.)

435
00:21:44,290 --> 00:21:46,260
I envy you. Give me some of your heat.

436
00:21:48,870 --> 00:21:52,170
If there's a good occasion for it, I'll do that.

437
00:21:54,070 --> 00:21:55,270
You'll be really surprised...

438
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:57,440
later when you...

439
00:21:58,310 --> 00:22:00,410
(A woman who needs warmth)

440
00:22:00,410 --> 00:22:02,980
(A man who needs to cool down)

441
00:22:05,680 --> 00:22:09,150
(At that time)

442
00:22:10,720 --> 00:22:11,820
I'm excited for them.

443
00:22:12,290 --> 00:22:15,320
You know what? Seon Ho and Ye Ji...

444
00:22:15,320 --> 00:22:17,090
- talk to each other a lot.
- Yes.

445
00:22:17,090 --> 00:22:18,900
I'm so curious about that.

446
00:22:21,960 --> 00:22:25,370
To be honest, I'm a bit bothered by Ye Ji.

447
00:22:25,370 --> 00:22:28,070
Well, hear me out.

448
00:22:28,340 --> 00:22:30,070
It's impossible not to be bothered by their history.

449
00:22:30,070 --> 00:22:33,510
He said that they talked online six years ago.

450
00:22:33,510 --> 00:22:34,910
When he doesn't express his interest,

451
00:22:34,910 --> 00:22:36,150
it's hard for us to approach him...

452
00:22:36,150 --> 00:22:37,880
- because their bond seems special.
- Of course.

453
00:22:39,020 --> 00:22:40,820
"We talked online six years ago."

454
00:22:41,150 --> 00:22:42,620
"But I'd like to get to know everyone."

455
00:22:42,620 --> 00:22:43,720
He should express that more.

456
00:22:43,720 --> 00:22:45,660
- But he's never been that open.
- Seon Ho doesn't talk.

457
00:22:45,660 --> 00:22:47,060
Right. It's natural for us...

458
00:22:47,060 --> 00:22:49,160
to assume he's only interested in Ye Ji and their history.

459
00:22:49,160 --> 00:22:51,130
- So we can't do anything.
- It sounds like a plot of a drama.

460
00:22:51,130 --> 00:22:52,500
- Right.
- Seriously.

461
00:22:52,500 --> 00:22:53,860
It's like they have to end up together.

462
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,530
That's why...

463
00:22:57,030 --> 00:23:00,170
(Their history from 6 years ago bothers her.)

464
00:23:01,170 --> 00:23:02,270
Right.

465
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:03,610
- Everyone was interested...
- Min Young too.

466
00:23:03,610 --> 00:23:05,470
in Seon Ho at first. He did bring that up.

467
00:23:05,810 --> 00:23:07,980
He told them about their history.

468
00:23:08,080 --> 00:23:09,210
I see. Right.

469
00:23:09,210 --> 00:23:11,950
After revealing everyone's age,

470
00:23:11,950 --> 00:23:13,350
Seon Ho was still on her mind.

471
00:23:13,350 --> 00:23:14,720
But they never had a chance to talk.

472
00:23:14,720 --> 00:23:17,950
And Na Young went on dates with other people.

473
00:23:18,320 --> 00:23:20,520
So she never got to go on a date with Seon Ho.

474
00:23:20,620 --> 00:23:23,790
My gosh. The thing is...

475
00:23:23,790 --> 00:23:26,300
I'm worried that he's meeting her after Ye Ji.

476
00:23:26,300 --> 00:23:28,000
- Right. That concerns me a lot.
- Yes.

477
00:23:29,170 --> 00:23:30,870
Earlier today, I asked her...

478
00:23:30,870 --> 00:23:32,100
how things were going for her.

479
00:23:32,100 --> 00:23:36,140
She made it sound like she had already made up her mind.

480
00:23:36,340 --> 00:23:38,310
(Turning)

481
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:41,710
She made it sound like it was almost official.

482
00:23:41,710 --> 00:23:42,750
- Ye Ji did?
- So...

483
00:23:43,110 --> 00:23:44,980
- Really?
- She said things were...

484
00:23:44,980 --> 00:23:46,180
- already decided.
- She did?

485
00:23:46,180 --> 00:23:48,120
- So...
- I think it depends on...

486
00:23:48,120 --> 00:23:49,190
- Seon Ho's decision.
- Of course.

487
00:23:49,190 --> 00:23:52,050
I think Seon Ho and Ye Ji will probably make things clear...

488
00:23:52,050 --> 00:23:53,790
during their date today.

489
00:23:53,790 --> 00:23:55,490
And he'll go on a date with you too.

490
00:23:55,490 --> 00:23:57,560
Afterward, things might get complicated for him.

491
00:23:57,830 --> 00:23:59,000
That's what I think.

492
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:01,700
My gosh. I don't want things to get complicated.

493
00:24:03,200 --> 00:24:05,770
I'm rooting for you. But anyway,

494
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:07,800
Seon Ho is also going on a date with you.

495
00:24:07,800 --> 00:24:11,540
Considering that, I think he's still open to other options.

496
00:24:11,640 --> 00:24:14,180
You should just have fun with him today.

497
00:24:14,180 --> 00:24:15,750
Show him how it is to date an older woman.

498
00:24:16,010 --> 00:24:18,980
I just need to hear a clear answer from him.

499
00:24:19,080 --> 00:24:21,050
- I want to know...
- I'm curious too.

500
00:24:21,050 --> 00:24:22,590
- what's on his mind.
- What is he thinking? Right.

501
00:24:23,050 --> 00:24:24,090
- Seriously.
- Yes.

502
00:24:24,550 --> 00:24:26,320
I'm so curious what he planned for your date.

503
00:24:27,160 --> 00:24:28,190
Right.

504
00:24:29,460 --> 00:24:30,490
I wonder what we'll do.

505
00:24:33,930 --> 00:24:35,400
(At that time)

506
00:24:35,800 --> 00:24:37,830
My gosh, how beautiful.

507
00:24:39,540 --> 00:24:40,600
Seriously.

508
00:24:41,370 --> 00:24:43,440
Aren't your feet sinking in too deep? Are you okay?

509
00:24:43,540 --> 00:24:44,670
This part is okay.

510
00:24:45,340 --> 00:24:46,940
What happens if I push you here?

511
00:24:46,940 --> 00:24:48,380
I don't think you can budge me.

512
00:24:49,980 --> 00:24:51,010
Really?

513
00:24:51,280 --> 00:24:52,750
I'm sorry. Was that the wrong answer?

514
00:24:53,820 --> 00:24:55,450
But I don't think I can budge you.

515
00:24:56,320 --> 00:24:58,790
I don't think you can budge me at all. So it'll be fine.

516
00:24:59,320 --> 00:25:03,160
The kids over there are throwing something at the seagulls.

517
00:25:03,160 --> 00:25:04,490
Do you see them gathering around?

518
00:25:06,760 --> 00:25:09,770
I heard that this would attract seagulls.

519
00:25:09,770 --> 00:25:10,830
Really?

520
00:25:10,830 --> 00:25:12,230
(Raising her hand)

521
00:25:14,270 --> 00:25:15,670
But that doesn't look right.

522
00:25:18,370 --> 00:25:20,910
(Ye Ji's finger is too tiny for a seagull to sit on.)

523
00:25:20,910 --> 00:25:21,940
How come they're not coming?

524
00:25:22,040 --> 00:25:24,010
They'd come, thinking we're holding out food.

525
00:25:24,110 --> 00:25:26,580
They're used to getting food from people now.

526
00:25:26,680 --> 00:25:29,250
That pose looks weird.

527
00:25:29,590 --> 00:25:32,390
It looks like you're trying to communicate with aliens.

528
00:25:32,390 --> 00:25:33,390
(Even a silly joke makes them laugh.)

529
00:25:34,660 --> 00:25:36,090
- How beautiful.
- It's beautiful.

530
00:25:36,090 --> 00:25:37,090
Yes.

531
00:25:39,630 --> 00:25:40,800
My gosh. Today...

532
00:25:41,230 --> 00:25:42,730
- The weather is amazing.
- Totally.

533
00:25:43,400 --> 00:25:46,040
Be honest. Do you think you can ever forget our date today?

534
00:25:46,040 --> 00:25:47,840
I liked it. I don't think I can ever forget it.

535
00:25:49,670 --> 00:25:52,610
But I had a great time on our previous dates too.

536
00:25:52,610 --> 00:25:53,610
- Right?
- Yes.

537
00:25:53,740 --> 00:25:56,310
But today's date has to be the best, hands down.

538
00:25:56,310 --> 00:25:58,580
It's nice to spend time together by the beach.

539
00:25:58,580 --> 00:25:59,620
- Yes.
- It's so beautiful here.

540
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:01,650
We should have breakfast together some time.

541
00:26:01,650 --> 00:26:03,090
- Sounds great.
- Right?

542
00:26:03,090 --> 00:26:05,120
We can't have it sometime. We only have two days left.

543
00:26:05,920 --> 00:26:07,790
- How about tomorrow?
- Tomorrow? Okay.

544
00:26:07,790 --> 00:26:09,430
- Promise?
- Promise. Okay.

545
00:26:09,430 --> 00:26:10,590
- Let's have breakfast tomorrow.
- Pinky promise.

546
00:26:12,900 --> 00:26:13,930
Okay.

547
00:26:14,360 --> 00:26:15,360
What should we eat?

548
00:26:15,630 --> 00:26:19,440
Breakfast tomorrow? How about an American brunch?

549
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,770
Yes, that sounds good.

550
00:26:23,740 --> 00:26:26,080
The light shimmering on the water is called "yunseul" in Korean, right?

551
00:26:26,180 --> 00:26:27,640
That's right.

552
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:29,510
This is the perfect way to zone out.

553
00:26:29,510 --> 00:26:31,880
- Right. Just gazing at the water.
- Yes.

554
00:26:33,350 --> 00:26:36,620
(The two of them stop in front of the ocean.)

555
00:26:37,320 --> 00:26:39,050
Looking at the water makes me so refreshed.

556
00:26:40,160 --> 00:26:41,760
- We're about the same height now.
- Hey.

557
00:26:43,390 --> 00:26:44,490
Who are you?

558
00:26:48,530 --> 00:26:49,530
This one is pretty.

559
00:26:51,630 --> 00:26:52,640
Right?

560
00:26:52,800 --> 00:26:54,800
- Should we take it?
- Should we?

561
00:26:54,800 --> 00:26:55,910
(Seon Ho picks up a clam shell.)

562
00:26:55,910 --> 00:26:57,140
Is there one more?

563
00:26:57,970 --> 00:26:59,510
This conch is cute too.

564
00:27:02,180 --> 00:27:03,350
What? No way.

565
00:27:03,350 --> 00:27:05,820
Did someone drop their souvenirs here?

566
00:27:06,580 --> 00:27:08,080
Which one do you want to keep?

567
00:27:11,690 --> 00:27:13,890
- It's beautiful.
- This one. Yes. It's so beautiful.

568
00:27:13,890 --> 00:27:14,890
Yes.

569
00:27:16,560 --> 00:27:17,560
It's so pretty.

570
00:27:17,560 --> 00:27:18,990
- It matches my outfit too.
- Yes, it does.

571
00:27:18,990 --> 00:27:20,200
- Right?
- Yes.

572
00:27:21,500 --> 00:27:23,230
Should we take a picture of them together?

573
00:27:23,230 --> 00:27:24,230
I'd love to.

574
00:27:26,340 --> 00:27:28,000
(They record their moment together.)

575
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:29,870
So I should...

576
00:27:32,370 --> 00:27:33,780
Is this in focus?

577
00:27:34,640 --> 00:27:36,480
(Covering her)

578
00:27:39,350 --> 00:27:40,420
Yes, I got it.

579
00:27:41,150 --> 00:27:42,650
- How beautiful.
- Yes.

580
00:27:45,320 --> 00:27:49,290
(A piece of their unforgettable day together)

581
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:53,460
People say you can hear the waves through it.

582
00:27:55,030 --> 00:27:56,330
- I can't.
- Okay.

583
00:27:57,630 --> 00:27:58,770
Do you want this?

584
00:27:58,770 --> 00:28:01,340
No. This one is pretty.

585
00:28:01,340 --> 00:28:02,370
- Right?
- Yes.

586
00:28:02,840 --> 00:28:06,380
It's like someone dropped their belongings here by accident.

587
00:28:06,380 --> 00:28:07,380
Right.

588
00:28:09,650 --> 00:28:12,580
Honestly, today's date felt like a scene in a movie.

589
00:28:13,150 --> 00:28:16,190
The date made me feel all fuzzy and cozy inside.

590
00:28:16,190 --> 00:28:18,590
I won't be able to forget every moment we spent together.

591
00:28:20,360 --> 00:28:21,960
That's the memorable part of my day.

592
00:28:23,730 --> 00:28:26,730
It felt like Seon Ho was my present.

593
00:28:26,730 --> 00:28:28,830
I realized today that...

594
00:28:28,830 --> 00:28:32,300
my feelings for Seon Ho were quite strong.

595
00:28:32,640 --> 00:28:35,870
That moment became unforgettable.

596
00:28:37,770 --> 00:28:39,210
What an interesting find.

597
00:28:39,210 --> 00:28:43,480
(An unforgettable page in their chapter together)

598
00:28:46,950 --> 00:28:48,980
- It looks so pretty over there.
- Yes.

599
00:28:49,750 --> 00:28:51,950
(Seon Ho gets a text message.)

600
00:28:54,849 --> 00:28:56,279
Could you keep this for me, please?

601
00:28:56,279 --> 00:28:57,949
- Sure.
- Thank you.

602
00:28:57,949 --> 00:28:59,919
(Kim Seon Ho's second date is waiting.)

603
00:28:59,919 --> 00:29:01,549
(Please go to the next location.)

604
00:29:01,730 --> 00:29:02,830
Right.

605
00:29:05,600 --> 00:29:07,400
I think we'll have to get going.

606
00:29:09,140 --> 00:29:10,240
- Let's head back to the car.
- This way?

607
00:29:10,240 --> 00:29:11,240
Yes.

608
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:13,670
(Ye Ji doesn't know about the message Seon Ho received.)

609
00:29:14,869 --> 00:29:16,299
I really like this.

610
00:29:23,779 --> 00:29:25,909
Ye Ji has no idea what's going on right now.

611
00:29:26,249 --> 00:29:29,149
- I feel frustrated.
- She'll think he's acting weird.

612
00:29:29,149 --> 00:29:31,019
Seon Ho must feel bad too.

613
00:29:31,319 --> 00:29:32,349
Goodness.

614
00:29:40,559 --> 00:29:41,659
Did you have a good time?

615
00:29:41,659 --> 00:29:43,799
Yes. What about you?

616
00:29:43,799 --> 00:29:45,869
I had a good time too. I had fun.

617
00:29:45,869 --> 00:29:47,529
- I enjoyed looking at the sea.
- Right.

618
00:29:49,839 --> 00:29:50,999
(Sighing)

619
00:29:53,109 --> 00:29:55,139
Look over there. The water is glistening.

620
00:29:57,539 --> 00:29:58,879
It's so pretty.

621
00:30:01,079 --> 00:30:02,319
That's very pretty.

622
00:30:02,679 --> 00:30:04,049
The tide came in a lot.

623
00:30:04,049 --> 00:30:05,049
Right.

624
00:30:05,049 --> 00:30:07,389
(The longest time they ever spent on each other...)

625
00:30:07,389 --> 00:30:09,689
(flew by faster than ever.)

626
00:30:12,629 --> 00:30:14,859
The beautiful moments passed by in the blink of an eye.

627
00:30:14,859 --> 00:30:17,829
- They really did.
- What I'm sure of is...

628
00:30:17,829 --> 00:30:19,569
that this date...

629
00:30:19,569 --> 00:30:22,199
would have had a really big impact on both of them.

630
00:30:22,199 --> 00:30:23,899
Seon Ho expressed himself a lot...

631
00:30:23,899 --> 00:30:25,569
- this time.
- Right.

632
00:30:25,569 --> 00:30:27,709
It feels like he's a lot more certain now.

633
00:30:27,709 --> 00:30:30,179
But if he really likes Na Young,

634
00:30:30,179 --> 00:30:32,379
and things keep progressing further,

635
00:30:32,379 --> 00:30:33,979
I think Ye Ji is going to have a really hard time.

636
00:30:33,979 --> 00:30:36,549
Ye Ji's feelings have reached 100 percent.

637
00:30:36,549 --> 00:30:38,849
- If I were Ye Ji, - Yes.

638
00:30:38,849 --> 00:30:41,089
- I'll say, "I'm out." - No.

639
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:43,259
That was what I was saying inside my head.

640
00:30:44,219 --> 00:30:47,089
- Ye Ji is certain right now.
- She is certain.

641
00:30:47,089 --> 00:30:49,029
Will Seon Ho's feelings for Na Young...

642
00:30:49,029 --> 00:30:51,659
grow more than 30 minutes...

643
00:30:51,659 --> 00:30:53,999
- We'll have to wait and see.
- Yes. We'll have to see.

644
00:30:53,999 --> 00:30:55,069
Really.

645
00:31:01,520 --> 00:31:04,950
While I was cleaning the kitchen today,

646
00:31:04,950 --> 00:31:07,450
I noticed there was a lot of laundry,

647
00:31:07,450 --> 00:31:11,060
so I asked where the washing machine was.

648
00:31:11,060 --> 00:31:14,060
The laundromat has a charm, you know.

649
00:31:14,060 --> 00:31:16,060
- Right...
- I've never been to a laundromat.

650
00:31:16,060 --> 00:31:18,100
I think I'd love to go to a laundromat...

651
00:31:18,100 --> 00:31:19,370
with someone I'm interested in.

652
00:31:19,370 --> 00:31:20,940
I used to go there a lot...

653
00:31:20,940 --> 00:31:22,200
- when I used to date.
- If you really like that person.

654
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:23,470
- Because...
- There's a charm to it.

655
00:31:23,470 --> 00:31:25,510
You spend a lot of time at the laundromat.

656
00:31:25,510 --> 00:31:26,670
It takes 40 minutes to wash...

657
00:31:26,670 --> 00:31:28,780
- and 40 minutes to dry.
- That's right.

658
00:31:28,780 --> 00:31:30,210
You'll get to talk...

659
00:31:30,210 --> 00:31:31,650
- for almost two hours.
- That's right.

660
00:31:31,650 --> 00:31:35,280
Does anyone want to go to the laundromat to do the laundry?

661
00:31:35,720 --> 00:31:37,180
(Reading the room)

662
00:31:37,180 --> 00:31:39,320
Then I'll...

663
00:31:39,320 --> 00:31:40,750
- Who do you want to go with?
- Ryun Gi?

664
00:31:40,750 --> 00:31:42,390
- Ryun Gi?
- Ryun Gi.

665
00:31:42,390 --> 00:31:43,390
I want to go there with him.

666
00:31:43,390 --> 00:31:45,790
I wanted to talk to him.

667
00:31:45,960 --> 00:31:48,000
Ro Bin feels comfortable only with Ryun Gi.

668
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:50,400
- Right? It's so nice to see that.
- She couldn't talk to others.

669
00:31:50,630 --> 00:31:51,930
Right?

670
00:31:54,270 --> 00:31:56,540
(Last night)

671
00:31:57,200 --> 00:31:59,340
If we get the time tomorrow,

672
00:31:59,340 --> 00:32:01,710
we could have a cup of tea...

673
00:32:01,710 --> 00:32:04,310
- That would be nice.
- and spend some time together.

674
00:32:04,310 --> 00:32:06,510
- That was what I had in mind.
- I'll need to sleep well tonight.

675
00:32:07,080 --> 00:32:09,950
(The short conversation led to a plan.)

676
00:32:10,150 --> 00:32:12,050
I had a brief time together...

677
00:32:12,050 --> 00:32:14,360
with Ryun Gi yesterday.

678
00:32:14,360 --> 00:32:17,090
He wanted us to hang out the next day.

679
00:32:17,090 --> 00:32:20,490
It made me want to talk to him more as well.

680
00:32:24,670 --> 00:32:26,570
Go and tell Ryun Gi now.

681
00:32:27,370 --> 00:32:28,370
(Rushing)

682
00:32:30,570 --> 00:32:31,870
(Determined)

683
00:32:32,640 --> 00:32:33,870
Ryun Gi.

684
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,340
Ryun...

685
00:32:37,340 --> 00:32:39,280
- Ryun Gi...
- Where's Ryun Gi?

686
00:32:39,280 --> 00:32:40,450
I'm looking for Ryun Gi.

687
00:32:40,450 --> 00:32:42,480
Where's Ryun Gi?

688
00:32:42,480 --> 00:32:43,550
Ryun Gi...

689
00:32:47,250 --> 00:32:48,290
He's not here.

690
00:32:48,290 --> 00:32:50,460
Ryun Gi, let's go to the laundromat.

691
00:32:50,460 --> 00:32:51,830
The laundry...

692
00:32:52,430 --> 00:32:54,260
You two can go to the laundromat.

693
00:32:54,260 --> 00:32:55,960
- The laundromat...
- But..

694
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:58,930
(Ryun Gi is trying to understand what's going on.)

695
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:00,400
Why did Do Gon appear...

696
00:33:00,400 --> 00:33:01,570
- of all people?
- I know, right?

697
00:33:02,300 --> 00:33:04,370
Do Gon looked for Ryun Gi with her.

698
00:33:04,840 --> 00:33:05,940
A shade.

699
00:33:05,940 --> 00:33:07,610
He couldn't be a better shade than that.

700
00:33:08,310 --> 00:33:10,480
For about three episodes,

701
00:33:10,480 --> 00:33:11,850
Do Gon has only shown us his shade.

702
00:33:13,010 --> 00:33:14,350
He's always...

703
00:33:14,350 --> 00:33:15,350
in places without any lighting.

704
00:33:15,350 --> 00:33:16,450
Right. It's so dark right now.

705
00:33:16,450 --> 00:33:18,320
They should have placed some lighting under him.

706
00:33:18,320 --> 00:33:20,550
He always stands in places without any lighting.

707
00:33:20,550 --> 00:33:22,560
- That's right.
- He's always listening.

708
00:33:22,720 --> 00:33:24,360
He's always like this.

709
00:33:24,830 --> 00:33:26,090
He'd be feeling nervous.

710
00:33:26,890 --> 00:33:29,500
- There's a lot of laundry piled up.
- We have to go there ourselves.

711
00:33:29,500 --> 00:33:30,700
That's right.

712
00:33:31,570 --> 00:33:33,900
It had nothing to do with my intentions.

713
00:33:33,900 --> 00:33:37,070
I guess she just wanted to go there with me.

714
00:33:37,070 --> 00:33:41,280
So I ended up going to do the laundry.

715
00:33:41,791 --> 00:33:44,421
It felt like I had become...

716
00:33:44,421 --> 00:33:47,291
a comfortable person to Ro Bin.

717
00:33:47,291 --> 00:33:49,301
I was really happy.

718
00:33:49,461 --> 00:33:50,731
Jong Eun and I will get some groceries...

719
00:33:50,731 --> 00:33:51,971
- Okay.
- Okay.

720
00:33:52,131 --> 00:33:53,231
and get the photos printed.

721
00:33:53,231 --> 00:33:55,141
Okay.

722
00:33:55,141 --> 00:33:57,671
You and I are going to the laundromat. Okay.

723
00:33:57,671 --> 00:34:00,141
(Ro Bin gets to spend some time with Ryun Gi.)

724
00:34:01,381 --> 00:34:02,581
- Jong Eun, let's...
- Yes.

725
00:34:02,581 --> 00:34:03,611
get the groceries together.

726
00:34:03,611 --> 00:34:04,951
- All right.
- We'll go grocery shopping...

727
00:34:04,951 --> 00:34:06,881
- Yes.
- and print the photos as well.

728
00:34:07,151 --> 00:34:09,021
I love spending time with you.

729
00:34:09,881 --> 00:34:11,651
- What?
- I'd like that.

730
00:34:12,751 --> 00:34:15,361
(Feeling bitter)

731
00:34:21,131 --> 00:34:23,061
- The weather is so nice.
- I know, right?

732
00:34:23,061 --> 00:34:24,401
It's a nice day to do the laundry.

733
00:34:24,571 --> 00:34:26,901
I want a scene...

734
00:34:26,901 --> 00:34:30,101
where we finish the laundry...

735
00:34:30,471 --> 00:34:32,741
and shake out the clothes and hang them up.

736
00:34:34,741 --> 00:34:35,841
I'm sorry.

737
00:34:36,981 --> 00:34:37,981
That's nice.

738
00:34:37,981 --> 00:34:39,711
Holding one side of the bag.

739
00:34:39,711 --> 00:34:41,551
It's got that vibe.

740
00:34:41,551 --> 00:34:42,721
The laundromat vibe.

741
00:34:43,181 --> 00:34:45,991
What do you think will happen to Ro Bin and Ryun Gi?

742
00:34:45,991 --> 00:34:47,321
Don't they look pretty nice?

743
00:34:47,321 --> 00:34:48,761
They seem comfortable.

744
00:34:48,761 --> 00:34:51,261
I think they might be confused. Their comfortable feeling...

745
00:34:51,261 --> 00:34:52,891
"Is it because I like that person?"

746
00:34:52,891 --> 00:34:55,661
"But I feel like we're more like friends."

747
00:34:55,661 --> 00:34:56,761
That's what they might be thinking.

748
00:34:56,761 --> 00:34:59,831
Do you think there isn't any chance?

749
00:34:59,831 --> 00:35:01,871
You never know what will happen.

750
00:35:01,871 --> 00:35:03,741
- They look good together.
- Really.

751
00:35:06,811 --> 00:35:08,281
I go to the laundromat once in a while.

752
00:35:08,281 --> 00:35:09,581
Amazing.

753
00:35:09,581 --> 00:35:13,211
(What will these two end up being to each other?)

754
00:35:14,651 --> 00:35:15,781
But...

755
00:35:15,781 --> 00:35:18,051
how did you end up going with me?

756
00:35:18,051 --> 00:35:20,151
- How was that decided?
- Well...

757
00:35:20,591 --> 00:35:22,291
I wanted to go there with you.

758
00:35:22,291 --> 00:35:24,831
- Really?
- I couldn't go on my own.

759
00:35:24,831 --> 00:35:28,061
We had a lot of towels piled up.

760
00:35:28,061 --> 00:35:29,101
Right.

761
00:35:31,501 --> 00:35:33,501
- Then let's...
- There's...

762
00:35:33,501 --> 00:35:36,271
a market nearby.

763
00:35:36,271 --> 00:35:39,111
Let's head to this parking lot first...

764
00:35:39,111 --> 00:35:40,511
and go from there.

765
00:35:42,041 --> 00:35:43,941
- We're here.
- Here? Okay.

766
00:35:45,481 --> 00:35:48,851
(They arrived at the neighborhood laundromat.)

767
00:35:51,181 --> 00:35:53,351
(The cozy scent of the laundromat on a sunny day)

768
00:35:53,351 --> 00:35:55,021
- Should we put them in?
- Yes.

769
00:35:57,121 --> 00:35:58,231
Let's put them in.

770
00:35:58,231 --> 00:36:00,631
Ro Bin, who's never lived on her own...

771
00:36:00,631 --> 00:36:02,531
Do we just put all of this in at once?

772
00:36:02,531 --> 00:36:03,831
- That's right.
- Right?

773
00:36:05,531 --> 00:36:08,871
(Ro Bin's first visit to the laundromat with Ryun Gi)

774
00:36:08,871 --> 00:36:09,941
It's falling down.

775
00:36:12,971 --> 00:36:14,071
It's done.

776
00:36:15,641 --> 00:36:16,741
Start.

777
00:36:18,351 --> 00:36:22,081
(The laundry is finally underway, thanks to Ryun Gi.)

778
00:36:25,291 --> 00:36:26,351
(Noticing something)

779
00:36:27,621 --> 00:36:29,121
The security camera.

780
00:36:29,121 --> 00:36:30,591
(The two caught on the security camera)

781
00:36:30,991 --> 00:36:32,991
Hold on. I brought the camera.

782
00:36:32,991 --> 00:36:35,531
(You look the prettiest when you're doing laundry.)

783
00:36:36,101 --> 00:36:37,531
- You brought the camera?
- Yes.

784
00:36:37,801 --> 00:36:39,201
The weather was so nice.

785
00:36:39,501 --> 00:36:41,271
Should we look over there?

786
00:36:50,111 --> 00:36:52,351
(When they're together, even a security camera...)

787
00:36:52,351 --> 00:36:54,611
(becomes a photo booth.)

788
00:36:56,151 --> 00:36:57,421
One, two, three.

789
00:36:57,421 --> 00:36:58,921
(They then take selfies.)

790
00:37:01,991 --> 00:37:04,291
Why did you stick your lips out?

791
00:37:04,291 --> 00:37:06,491
(Why did you stick your lips out?)

792
00:37:06,731 --> 00:37:09,231
- Are you commenting on my face?
- No...

793
00:37:09,231 --> 00:37:11,371
I like being taught like that.

794
00:37:12,201 --> 00:37:13,571
- Hold on.
- Smile.

795
00:37:14,331 --> 00:37:15,501
(Smiling)

796
00:37:16,041 --> 00:37:17,141
Don't stick your lips out.

797
00:37:17,141 --> 00:37:18,271
Tell me what to do.

798
00:37:20,971 --> 00:37:24,141
(They take another selfie following Ro Bin's instructions.)

799
00:37:28,121 --> 00:37:29,321
That looks good.

800
00:37:29,381 --> 00:37:31,021
- Do you like it?
- I like it.

801
00:37:31,791 --> 00:37:34,591
I want to have something to remember everyone by.

802
00:37:34,591 --> 00:37:35,591
That would be nice.

803
00:37:35,591 --> 00:37:36,991
I think I'll feel sad later.

804
00:37:37,791 --> 00:37:39,431
Why is it so small?

805
00:37:39,431 --> 00:37:42,201
(Ro Bin and Ryun Gi are waiting for the laundry to be done outside.)

806
00:37:43,361 --> 00:37:44,461
The weather is so nice today.

807
00:37:44,461 --> 00:37:46,031
It's so nice that it's not cold.

808
00:37:46,031 --> 00:37:48,141
It was quite cold yesterday.

809
00:37:48,141 --> 00:37:51,301
There's less wind. It's nice.

810
00:37:51,301 --> 00:37:52,441
Right.

811
00:37:52,441 --> 00:37:53,741
(Smiling)

812
00:37:57,041 --> 00:37:58,511
That's so cute. It's a cycling crew.

813
00:37:59,651 --> 00:38:00,781
What's that?

814
00:38:01,281 --> 00:38:02,421
(Laughing)

815
00:38:06,651 --> 00:38:08,291
- That's cute.
- It is cute.

816
00:38:08,291 --> 00:38:09,321
It's funny.

817
00:38:09,991 --> 00:38:11,061
What's that?

818
00:38:12,331 --> 00:38:14,361
- They're showing it to us.
- It was natural.

819
00:38:14,931 --> 00:38:16,001
They're showing it to us.

820
00:38:17,201 --> 00:38:18,201
Did you see that?

821
00:38:18,601 --> 00:38:20,201
He's riding it sideways.

822
00:38:20,201 --> 00:38:21,401
Doesn't it hurt?

823
00:38:21,871 --> 00:38:24,641
(The audience is loving it.)

824
00:38:25,211 --> 00:38:27,271
- Seriously.
- You know, when you're young,

825
00:38:27,471 --> 00:38:30,241
- What?
- there are kids who ride...

826
00:38:30,241 --> 00:38:32,081
without using their hands...

827
00:38:32,151 --> 00:38:34,651
- trying to look cool.
- That's right.

828
00:38:34,651 --> 00:38:36,121
(Bringing back childhood memories)

829
00:38:36,281 --> 00:38:38,391
I lived in the countryside.

830
00:38:38,951 --> 00:38:41,351
I lived in Uhm Bok Dong's neighborhood.

831
00:38:41,691 --> 00:38:43,561
Once you get a bicycle, it disappears.

832
00:38:44,061 --> 00:38:45,791
Right. That would be the case.

833
00:38:46,091 --> 00:38:48,801
I don't think people will keep it locked.

834
00:38:48,801 --> 00:38:50,301
It becomes a shared bicycle.

835
00:38:51,801 --> 00:38:53,101
A shared bicycle?

836
00:38:53,471 --> 00:38:55,541
You rent the Ttareungi bikes in Seoul.

837
00:38:55,541 --> 00:38:56,841
Back there, all bicycles were Ttareungi bikes.

838
00:38:59,111 --> 00:39:01,411
Did they come back someday?

839
00:39:01,511 --> 00:39:03,981
You'll notice it while passing by. "That's my bicycle!"

840
00:39:04,211 --> 00:39:06,411
"Hold on. It is mine."

841
00:39:06,951 --> 00:39:08,081
Really?

842
00:39:08,381 --> 00:39:10,521
- Really.
- I like that.

843
00:39:10,881 --> 00:39:12,291
I want something like that.

844
00:39:12,891 --> 00:39:14,691
That's the countryside life.

845
00:39:14,961 --> 00:39:15,961
Right.

846
00:39:16,391 --> 00:39:17,591
That's so funny.

847
00:39:18,661 --> 00:39:20,861
I feel the most comfortable talking to you.

848
00:39:21,091 --> 00:39:23,061
- Really?
- Don't you feel that?

849
00:39:24,501 --> 00:39:26,931
You shouldn't get too comfortable though.

850
00:39:26,931 --> 00:39:28,741
But I like this.

851
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:30,801
- Really? That sort of vibe?
- I like it.

852
00:39:34,271 --> 00:39:36,541
There's that thing.

853
00:39:37,341 --> 00:39:39,111
That's why it's hard for me.

854
00:39:39,111 --> 00:39:42,421
When seeing you romantically...

855
00:39:42,751 --> 00:39:45,921
The relationships I've wanted...

856
00:39:46,351 --> 00:39:49,961
have always started out feeling this comfortable.

857
00:39:52,531 --> 00:39:55,601
If we were living our everyday lives,

858
00:39:56,131 --> 00:39:57,661
we would have enough time.

859
00:39:57,761 --> 00:39:59,501
- But we have seven days.
- Right.

860
00:39:59,501 --> 00:40:02,771
So if I'm to express my feelings to you once they develop,

861
00:40:03,101 --> 00:40:05,641
that comfortable feeling wouldn't help.

862
00:40:06,211 --> 00:40:07,941
- Right.
- That kept me thinking.

863
00:40:08,041 --> 00:40:10,211
What should I do...

864
00:40:11,211 --> 00:40:13,311
if I like Ro Bin?

865
00:40:13,311 --> 00:40:15,851
Would I need to break out of that comfort zone?

866
00:40:17,781 --> 00:40:18,921
What do you think?

867
00:40:19,321 --> 00:40:20,691
(She's startled.)

868
00:40:21,991 --> 00:40:22,991
What?

869
00:40:22,991 --> 00:40:24,121
- What?
- What?

870
00:40:24,391 --> 00:40:26,491
He's saying, "What can I do..."

871
00:40:26,491 --> 00:40:27,861
- To capture her heart.
- "to earn your heart?"

872
00:40:27,861 --> 00:40:29,931
Right. I think that's what he meant.

873
00:40:30,201 --> 00:40:32,801
I think he made it clear to Ro Bin.

874
00:40:32,801 --> 00:40:34,231
- That's so cool.
- That's right.

875
00:40:34,231 --> 00:40:35,571
He's really honest.

876
00:40:36,041 --> 00:40:37,101
It feels comfortable.

877
00:40:37,201 --> 00:40:38,571
(Self-service laundromat)

878
00:40:38,571 --> 00:40:40,871
Would you need something else?

879
00:40:40,941 --> 00:40:41,981
No.

880
00:40:42,311 --> 00:40:44,081
- You don't need anything else?
- That's right.

881
00:40:44,081 --> 00:40:45,851
You can just do what you're doing.

882
00:40:45,851 --> 00:40:48,321
(You can just do what you're doing.)

883
00:40:52,021 --> 00:40:57,861
(Ro Bin tells him that he's enough just as he is.)

884
00:41:04,261 --> 00:41:05,271
Why?

885
00:41:08,231 --> 00:41:12,571
Actually, while talking to her,

886
00:41:13,071 --> 00:41:15,311
I think I was curious...

887
00:41:15,311 --> 00:41:17,311
to know how she was processing her feelings.

888
00:41:17,581 --> 00:41:21,151
I could tell from that conversation that...

889
00:41:21,151 --> 00:41:23,551
she didn't feel much differently before and after I got sick.

890
00:41:23,821 --> 00:41:26,691
The people I used to like were like this.

891
00:41:30,161 --> 00:41:32,931
This is the kind of relationship I've always wanted.

892
00:41:33,161 --> 00:41:35,061
I told you.

893
00:41:35,361 --> 00:41:37,131
A stable and comfortable relationship.

894
00:41:39,471 --> 00:41:40,801
To me,

895
00:41:40,801 --> 00:41:45,271
that made things more romantic.

896
00:41:50,441 --> 00:41:52,551
- I wanted to ask you this.
- What is it?

897
00:41:53,681 --> 00:41:56,021
You spent time with me before,

898
00:41:56,221 --> 00:41:59,251
but I was all over the place that day.

899
00:41:59,821 --> 00:42:02,091
I felt bad about how that date went.

900
00:42:02,161 --> 00:42:03,721
Really? Right, that's true.

901
00:42:04,021 --> 00:42:05,331
I felt bad about it too.

902
00:42:05,431 --> 00:42:07,331
It was so awkward.

903
00:42:07,991 --> 00:42:10,131
I was with you, and I was talking to you,

904
00:42:10,431 --> 00:42:12,371
- but I also had to look at the map.
- Right.

905
00:42:12,501 --> 00:42:14,701
- The road was also rough.
- That's right.

906
00:42:14,901 --> 00:42:16,241
I really couldn't focus.

907
00:42:16,701 --> 00:42:17,801
- So...
- I can imagine.

908
00:42:18,541 --> 00:42:21,171
I felt bad about that.

909
00:42:21,471 --> 00:42:23,381
I wanted to know...

910
00:42:23,381 --> 00:42:25,281
what you felt about that time.

911
00:42:26,651 --> 00:42:28,521
- Honestly?
- Yes.

912
00:42:29,081 --> 00:42:31,381
- About our date?
- Yes.

913
00:42:32,451 --> 00:42:33,951
I liked it. I liked it, but...

914
00:42:34,351 --> 00:42:36,661
since we were outside as well,

915
00:42:38,221 --> 00:42:40,961
I also couldn't focus much on our conversations.

916
00:42:43,301 --> 00:42:44,301
Right.

917
00:42:44,561 --> 00:42:46,071
You felt that as well.

918
00:42:48,701 --> 00:42:51,671
- You too?
- You too?

919
00:42:52,841 --> 00:42:53,871
Right.

920
00:42:54,211 --> 00:42:55,511
That's why...

921
00:42:55,941 --> 00:42:56,981
I knew it.

922
00:42:57,781 --> 00:42:59,851
That's why I wanted...

923
00:42:59,851 --> 00:43:03,551
to spend time like that together again.

924
00:43:03,551 --> 00:43:04,581
Right.

925
00:43:05,551 --> 00:43:08,121
But I said things like that.

926
00:43:09,461 --> 00:43:11,791
(During their first date)

927
00:43:13,461 --> 00:43:17,301
(Honestly speaking, your treatment is still ongoing.)

928
00:43:17,531 --> 00:43:20,131
(When I considered that,)

929
00:43:20,131 --> 00:43:21,801
(it gave me more thoughts.)

930
00:43:21,801 --> 00:43:24,701
(I'd need more time to think about things.)

931
00:43:27,841 --> 00:43:30,811
I think I was too honest with you.

932
00:43:30,811 --> 00:43:32,851
- But that didn't become an issue.
- Really?

933
00:43:32,851 --> 00:43:35,121
I wasn't shocked by that.

934
00:43:35,621 --> 00:43:37,781
I came here...

935
00:43:38,081 --> 00:43:41,491
to sort out those thoughts.

936
00:43:43,091 --> 00:43:44,891
You just reminded me of that.

937
00:43:45,161 --> 00:43:47,261
But that's something I had to do.

938
00:43:47,261 --> 00:43:49,261
If I hadn't sorted out those things,

939
00:43:51,331 --> 00:43:53,171
I would have been...

940
00:43:54,431 --> 00:43:55,541
struggling with that until the end.

941
00:43:56,671 --> 00:43:59,711
That's why I thought I should talk with you again today.

942
00:43:59,911 --> 00:44:01,441
Since we were at the house.

943
00:44:04,481 --> 00:44:07,911
I thought it would be nice to have another conversation.

944
00:44:08,621 --> 00:44:10,351
(Nodding)

945
00:44:13,151 --> 00:44:14,891
I kept feeling bad...

946
00:44:15,491 --> 00:44:17,391
about that day.

947
00:44:17,961 --> 00:44:19,731
I feel so refreshed.

948
00:44:21,801 --> 00:44:26,871
To me, those honest words by Ro Bin...

949
00:44:27,401 --> 00:44:31,201
became a chance for me to sort my thoughts out.

950
00:44:31,501 --> 00:44:33,471
I was very grateful for that.

951
00:44:33,771 --> 00:44:35,541
But Ro Bin...

952
00:44:36,281 --> 00:44:40,011
was worried that her words might have hurt me.

953
00:44:40,611 --> 00:44:43,751
She still seemed to be bothered by that.

954
00:44:43,921 --> 00:44:45,721
So I made sure...

955
00:44:46,221 --> 00:44:49,921
to tell her that I was really thankful to her.

956
00:44:50,791 --> 00:44:53,431
I was regretting the words I said,

957
00:44:53,731 --> 00:44:55,401
but he was thankful for them.

958
00:44:55,961 --> 00:44:59,071
Ryun Gi really sees me as a good person.

959
00:44:59,601 --> 00:45:02,201
That made me really thankful to him.

960
00:45:04,501 --> 00:45:06,541
I've talked...

961
00:45:06,541 --> 00:45:08,311
to many people.

962
00:45:08,471 --> 00:45:10,081
I'm experiencing...

963
00:45:10,081 --> 00:45:12,511
many trials and errors through that.

964
00:45:12,911 --> 00:45:16,351
I think things are getting sorted out bit by bit.

965
00:45:16,351 --> 00:45:17,421
I see.

966
00:45:17,881 --> 00:45:18,921
That's what's happening.

967
00:45:19,621 --> 00:45:22,861
Can I ask you how they're being sorted out?

968
00:45:24,891 --> 00:45:25,931
Well...

969
00:45:28,091 --> 00:45:30,831
"This is a bit different from what I thought."

970
00:45:31,331 --> 00:45:33,831
My thoughts are changing in that way...

971
00:45:34,031 --> 00:45:36,041
for things I was sure I was certain of.

972
00:45:36,541 --> 00:45:37,671
They're changing.

973
00:45:38,711 --> 00:45:41,411
So I want...

974
00:45:42,703 --> 00:45:46,373
I want to take another look at someone else.

975
00:45:46,373 --> 00:45:48,443
(I want to take another look at someone else.)

976
00:45:49,513 --> 00:45:50,783
- Goodness.
- What?

977
00:45:50,783 --> 00:45:52,683
- Will Ro Bin change her mind?
- Will she change her mind?

978
00:45:53,213 --> 00:45:56,423
Ro Bin noticed that Jong Eun...

979
00:45:56,423 --> 00:45:57,983
- doesn't have feelings for her.
- That's right.

980
00:45:57,983 --> 00:45:59,793
Also, she said...

981
00:46:00,023 --> 00:46:01,523
she feels most comfortable...

982
00:46:01,523 --> 00:46:02,793
around Ryun Gi.

983
00:46:02,793 --> 00:46:04,623
That felt like...

984
00:46:04,623 --> 00:46:06,133
- it had some meaning.
- Right.

985
00:46:07,193 --> 00:46:09,603
It looks like things might change.

986
00:46:09,603 --> 00:46:11,233
- That might be possible.
- Right.

987
00:46:11,233 --> 00:46:12,733
What could it be?

988
00:46:14,373 --> 00:46:16,603
(Ro Bin's certain feelings...)

989
00:46:16,603 --> 00:46:18,613
(started shaking.)

990
00:46:19,473 --> 00:46:21,373
Once today ends,

991
00:46:21,373 --> 00:46:24,283
we're only left with two days, right?

992
00:46:24,543 --> 00:46:26,253
That's right.

993
00:46:26,383 --> 00:46:28,313
Time really flies.

994
00:46:29,883 --> 00:46:31,423
So fast.

995
00:46:31,423 --> 00:46:34,523
(They only have two days left.)

996
00:46:35,663 --> 00:46:37,363
Do you think you won't regret this?

997
00:46:38,693 --> 00:46:41,333
I won't. I've learned so much already.

998
00:46:42,505 --> 00:46:45,345
Me too. I think I'll be cringing about this a lot later.

999
00:46:46,381 --> 00:46:48,181
But I don't think I'll regret it.

1000
00:46:48,481 --> 00:46:50,211
I've learned so much.

1001
00:46:50,951 --> 00:46:53,181
I also learned so much.

1002
00:46:54,521 --> 00:46:57,591
I've learned a lot about my feelings.

1003
00:46:57,591 --> 00:47:00,191
Like, "What kind of feeling is this?"

1004
00:47:00,761 --> 00:47:02,391
"So this is what this feeling is."

1005
00:47:02,391 --> 00:47:04,531
I had so many of such things.

1006
00:47:04,531 --> 00:47:05,631
(Feelings Ro Bin, who's never dated, has never felt before)

1007
00:47:09,661 --> 00:47:11,531
I was diagnosed...

1008
00:47:11,531 --> 00:47:14,261
in November, 2025,

1009
00:47:15,531 --> 00:47:17,171
- so it's not even been half a year.
- Yes.

1010
00:47:17,971 --> 00:47:19,671
It hasn't been so long...

1011
00:47:19,671 --> 00:47:21,771
- since I started chemotherapy.
- Right.

1012
00:47:21,771 --> 00:47:25,381
So I'm in the process where...

1013
00:47:25,381 --> 00:47:28,341
I'm forming a new sense of self and new values.

1014
00:47:28,341 --> 00:47:30,011
- That's right.
- I think...

1015
00:47:30,011 --> 00:47:32,281
- it got formed after I got here.
- Right.

1016
00:47:32,281 --> 00:47:34,651
It's also really amazing...

1017
00:47:34,781 --> 00:47:36,821
how you came here in the process of all that.

1018
00:47:37,321 --> 00:47:39,021
I think you're really cool.

1019
00:47:39,021 --> 00:47:41,361
I wouldn't be able to come here.

1020
00:47:42,661 --> 00:47:43,791
That's really amazing.

1021
00:47:46,601 --> 00:47:47,601
Is that so?

1022
00:47:47,601 --> 00:47:49,331
Of course!

1023
00:47:49,901 --> 00:47:52,741
You're the most amazing person here.

1024
00:47:53,071 --> 00:47:54,101
Come on.

1025
00:47:54,771 --> 00:47:56,241
Whenever I'm with anyone here,

1026
00:47:56,241 --> 00:47:57,771
including you,

1027
00:47:58,411 --> 00:48:01,141
I keep...

1028
00:48:01,681 --> 00:48:02,681
What is it?

1029
00:48:02,681 --> 00:48:05,651
I keep forgetting that I'm sick.

1030
00:48:05,651 --> 00:48:07,021
- Really?
- Yes.

1031
00:48:07,021 --> 00:48:08,691
That's really important, you know?

1032
00:48:09,791 --> 00:48:11,391
- The thing is, - Yes?

1033
00:48:11,391 --> 00:48:14,121
I'm not sure if this is okay.

1034
00:48:14,121 --> 00:48:16,031
I forget it to the point where it worries me.

1035
00:48:16,761 --> 00:48:18,091
But that's great.

1036
00:48:18,091 --> 00:48:20,731
- When I talk to you, - Yes?

1037
00:48:20,731 --> 00:48:22,501
I keep forgetting that I'm sick.

1038
00:48:22,601 --> 00:48:24,131
That's something really important.

1039
00:48:24,131 --> 00:48:25,901
- I come around once it's evening.
- Nice.

1040
00:48:25,901 --> 00:48:26,901
How come?

1041
00:48:27,171 --> 00:48:28,501
"Oh, right. I was sick."

1042
00:48:28,601 --> 00:48:30,171
I see.

1043
00:48:30,171 --> 00:48:32,611
But you forget about it at least for this moment?

1044
00:48:32,841 --> 00:48:33,841
Yes.

1045
00:48:36,311 --> 00:48:39,251
- That's awesome.
- It's totally awesome.

1046
00:48:39,551 --> 00:48:41,521
"I forget when I talk to you."

1047
00:48:41,721 --> 00:48:43,391
Anyone would be happy to hear that.

1048
00:48:43,391 --> 00:48:44,451
How sweet of him.

1049
00:48:44,551 --> 00:48:46,391
Ryun Gi needs Ro Bin.

1050
00:48:46,391 --> 00:48:48,861
- Ro Bin is someone he needs.
- For sure.

1051
00:48:48,861 --> 00:48:51,631
I'm grateful that you feel that way.

1052
00:48:52,301 --> 00:48:54,861
- Me?
- It's nice to hear that in words.

1053
00:48:56,671 --> 00:48:57,731
I'm the grateful one.

1054
00:48:57,731 --> 00:49:00,741
I'm grateful to the people who make me feel like that.

1055
00:49:03,171 --> 00:49:05,311
Gosh, I'm glad I came out to do my laundry.

1056
00:49:05,311 --> 00:49:07,611
Right? But weren't you taken aback when I said,

1057
00:49:07,611 --> 00:49:11,011
"Ryun Gi, we have to go do the laundry" without any heads-up?

1058
00:49:11,011 --> 00:49:12,621
Yes. I was surprised, like, "What?"

1059
00:49:13,151 --> 00:49:16,091
(Ro Bin's laundromat mission made the day special.)

1060
00:49:22,261 --> 00:49:25,131
(While the two chat about different topics)

1061
00:49:25,661 --> 00:49:28,971
(Looking around)

1062
00:49:28,971 --> 00:49:31,231
- I think it's done.
- Is it?

1063
00:49:34,671 --> 00:49:35,671
Or not?

1064
00:49:36,211 --> 00:49:37,311
- It's done.
- It's done.

1065
00:49:41,781 --> 00:49:47,921
(Ro Bin and Ryun Gi's laundromat date has ended!)

1066
00:49:48,321 --> 00:49:49,451
(Meanwhile)

1067
00:49:52,161 --> 00:49:53,161
Thank you.

1068
00:49:53,161 --> 00:49:56,791
(The two are back with both hands full from grocery shopping.)

1069
00:49:59,501 --> 00:50:00,701
No, I'll do it.

1070
00:50:00,701 --> 00:50:04,931
(They're going to make dinner.)

1071
00:50:04,931 --> 00:50:06,201
Let's go.

1072
00:50:06,941 --> 00:50:09,971
(Main Chef Do Gon)

1073
00:50:10,071 --> 00:50:13,011
(Sous-Chef Jong Eun)

1074
00:50:13,011 --> 00:50:14,381
Could you add just enough water...

1075
00:50:14,381 --> 00:50:16,511
- to cover the meat?
- Sure.

1076
00:50:17,181 --> 00:50:18,311
- I'm sorry.
- Hey.

1077
00:50:18,311 --> 00:50:19,321
(Splashing)

1078
00:50:19,321 --> 00:50:20,951
- I'm sorry.
- Hey. Was it on purpose?

1079
00:50:20,951 --> 00:50:23,321
No, it wasn't on purpose. Really.

1080
00:50:23,321 --> 00:50:24,491
(Even with the splashes, they're all smiles.)

1081
00:50:24,591 --> 00:50:27,021
Do you often cook suyuk at home?

1082
00:50:27,291 --> 00:50:28,761
- I do.
- Really?

1083
00:50:28,761 --> 00:50:29,761
That's good.

1084
00:50:33,431 --> 00:50:35,531
(Ssanghwatang)

1085
00:50:36,631 --> 00:50:37,801
(Bay leaves)

1086
00:50:38,531 --> 00:50:39,971
(Ssamjang)

1087
00:50:40,171 --> 00:50:43,041
(Do Gon cooks suyuk like it's nothing using his secret recipe.)

1088
00:50:43,141 --> 00:50:45,781
(Boiling)

1089
00:50:45,781 --> 00:50:47,911
Totally. It's nice.

1090
00:50:47,911 --> 00:50:51,111
(Meanwhile, Ryun Gi and Ro Bin are back.)

1091
00:50:51,551 --> 00:50:52,581
Let's fold the laundry...

1092
00:50:52,581 --> 00:50:53,621
- in the living room first.
- Okay.

1093
00:50:53,881 --> 00:50:56,691
You know, without exception, I...

1094
00:51:04,391 --> 00:51:05,761
Folding the clothes...

1095
00:51:07,761 --> 00:51:10,771
is making me feel like I'm at my family home.

1096
00:51:11,131 --> 00:51:12,141
Right?

1097
00:51:12,141 --> 00:51:14,301
I love it when the clothes are warm...

1098
00:51:14,301 --> 00:51:17,111
when I touch them. Don't you?

1099
00:51:18,111 --> 00:51:20,111
How do you fold your socks?

1100
00:51:20,111 --> 00:51:21,211
This is how I do it.

1101
00:51:21,211 --> 00:51:22,711
- Really?
- But it doesn't look right.

1102
00:51:23,211 --> 00:51:24,751
It's okay. Those are my socks.

1103
00:51:24,751 --> 00:51:26,651
Seriously? No, I'll fold them like this.

1104
00:51:26,981 --> 00:51:28,221
- Oh, my.
- Like so.

1105
00:51:28,721 --> 00:51:30,421
- You're going that far for them?
- Good?

1106
00:51:30,521 --> 00:51:31,791
- Let's go.
- Okay.

1107
00:51:32,991 --> 00:51:34,061
Your socks.

1108
00:51:35,491 --> 00:51:37,991
I love this pair. They're cute.

1109
00:51:37,991 --> 00:51:40,701
(While Ryun Gi and Ro Bin are folding the laundry,)

1110
00:51:41,961 --> 00:51:43,531
(dinner is still being prepped in the kitchen.)

1111
00:51:43,531 --> 00:51:45,571
- Maybe Heineken?
- Was it Heineken?

1112
00:51:45,571 --> 00:51:47,271
I think it was a Japanese beer.

1113
00:51:47,271 --> 00:51:48,701
No, Japanese beers are...

1114
00:51:48,701 --> 00:51:50,111
- It was red.
- Who's there?

1115
00:51:50,111 --> 00:51:52,111
- It could be Asahi.
- Asahi seems right.

1116
00:51:52,581 --> 00:51:53,781
How far are you into cooking?

1117
00:51:54,241 --> 00:51:55,311
All that's left is for it to boil.

1118
00:51:55,881 --> 00:51:58,051
(Amazed)

1119
00:51:58,051 --> 00:51:59,681
Ryun Gi, which laundromat did you use?

1120
00:51:59,781 --> 00:52:02,081
There was one a minute away from here.

1121
00:52:02,081 --> 00:52:05,021
But waiting for the laundry to get done took ages.

1122
00:52:05,021 --> 00:52:06,821
- Did you wait at the laundromat?
- Yes.

1123
00:52:06,921 --> 00:52:09,191
We waited while chatting.

1124
00:52:09,191 --> 00:52:11,891
How did it go? Didn't you have something to tell her?

1125
00:52:11,891 --> 00:52:13,761
Yes. We talked.

1126
00:52:13,861 --> 00:52:17,801
The conversation helped clear the air.

1127
00:52:18,431 --> 00:52:20,341
- Well done.
- Talking to her was worth it.

1128
00:52:21,441 --> 00:52:23,841
The day ended in a flash without me doing much.

1129
00:52:23,841 --> 00:52:26,741
(Ryun Gi talks about his day spent with Ro Bin.)

1130
00:52:30,081 --> 00:52:35,181
(Do Gon's time is ticking away in anxiety.)

1131
00:52:35,521 --> 00:52:37,621
Oh, no. What should he do?

1132
00:52:38,021 --> 00:52:39,091
Do Gon started off as...

1133
00:52:39,091 --> 00:52:40,591
- Hundred Do Gon, - Exactly.

1134
00:52:40,591 --> 00:52:43,061
- Straightforward Do Gon, and more.
- Pitter-patter Do Gon.

1135
00:52:43,161 --> 00:52:44,761
Now, he's giving off Gloomy Do Gon.

1136
00:52:44,761 --> 00:52:46,431
- Gloomy Do Gon.
- Gloomy Do Gon?

1137
00:52:46,431 --> 00:52:47,561
This is heartbreaking.

1138
00:52:47,561 --> 00:52:49,101
Do Gon doesn't want to put pressure on her,

1139
00:52:49,201 --> 00:52:51,201
but he only wants to choose her.

1140
00:52:51,201 --> 00:52:53,341
Nothing can be done, which is frustrating.

1141
00:52:53,341 --> 00:52:54,371
Indeed.

1142
00:52:54,371 --> 00:52:55,611
(Mixed feelings)

1143
00:53:00,601 --> 00:53:03,761
(Ye Ji has returned alone after the date.)

1144
00:53:09,641 --> 00:53:12,641
(After changing into comfy clothes,)

1145
00:53:13,111 --> 00:53:15,711
(she runs into Ro Bin.)

1146
00:53:15,981 --> 00:53:17,651
What did you do today?

1147
00:53:19,111 --> 00:53:22,251
Ryun Gi. We went to the laundromat together and talked.

1148
00:53:22,621 --> 00:53:25,121
Have you settled on someone or something?

1149
00:53:25,651 --> 00:53:28,891
The conversation I had with Ryun Gi today was great.

1150
00:53:29,161 --> 00:53:30,221
I felt at ease.

1151
00:53:30,461 --> 00:53:31,991
Ryun Gi is very expressive.

1152
00:53:32,091 --> 00:53:33,491
Because he's very expressive...

1153
00:53:33,491 --> 00:53:34,561
- He's a nice guy.
- Right? I know...

1154
00:53:34,561 --> 00:53:36,061
what he's thinking right then and there.

1155
00:53:37,062 --> 00:53:38,902
The talk was great.

1156
00:53:40,672 --> 00:53:44,172
But he turned out to be different from...

1157
00:53:45,623 --> 00:53:47,163
what I had expected.

1158
00:53:50,063 --> 00:53:53,903
(Her feelings toward Ryun Gi are still hard to explain.)

1159
00:53:54,433 --> 00:53:56,303
So how was today's date?

1160
00:53:56,973 --> 00:53:59,473
Today's date? I had fun.

1161
00:53:59,473 --> 00:54:01,243
You did? Are you happy with the talks?

1162
00:54:02,073 --> 00:54:04,083
- We went to the beach.
- Seriously?

1163
00:54:04,583 --> 00:54:06,413
For real? How far is the beach from here?

1164
00:54:06,943 --> 00:54:07,983
It's an hour away.

1165
00:54:08,383 --> 00:54:11,523
I was shocked. "Are we really going to the beach from here?"

1166
00:54:12,083 --> 00:54:13,123
I'm jealous.

1167
00:54:13,123 --> 00:54:15,093
Was it windy at the beach? How was it?

1168
00:54:15,193 --> 00:54:18,123
We had grilled clams outdoors.

1169
00:54:18,723 --> 00:54:21,193
It was a little breezy, like so.

1170
00:54:21,993 --> 00:54:23,893
- "Breezy." - "Breezy."

1171
00:54:23,893 --> 00:54:25,963
- "Breezy." - "It was a little breezy, like so?"

1172
00:54:25,963 --> 00:54:27,373
It wasn't even a lot.

1173
00:54:27,373 --> 00:54:29,133
- "Breezy, like so." - Breezy.

1174
00:54:30,903 --> 00:54:33,303
- Look how happy she is.
- Come on and tell her already.

1175
00:54:33,573 --> 00:54:35,073
Tell her he has another date.

1176
00:54:35,073 --> 00:54:36,073
Should I tell her now?

1177
00:54:36,173 --> 00:54:38,783
- Ye Ji!
- Ye Ji, this is Yong Hwa.

1178
00:54:39,783 --> 00:54:40,983
Smile a little less.

1179
00:54:41,753 --> 00:54:42,813
Don't smile too much.

1180
00:54:43,053 --> 00:54:44,253
Smile about 70 percent.

1181
00:54:44,253 --> 00:54:45,923
- Don't smile yet.
- No, don't smile yet.

1182
00:54:46,523 --> 00:54:47,593
That's hilarious.

1183
00:54:48,123 --> 00:54:50,663
It was a little breezy, like so.

1184
00:54:51,093 --> 00:54:52,763
- It must've been nice.
- It was really nice.

1185
00:54:52,763 --> 00:54:54,033
- The clams sound delicious.
- Right?

1186
00:54:54,533 --> 00:54:55,993
The clams were amazing.

1187
00:54:56,563 --> 00:54:59,363
We devoured them. We emptied every clam.

1188
00:55:00,603 --> 00:55:03,973
(A little while later)

1189
00:55:05,503 --> 00:55:09,043
(Doing the dishes before eating dinner)

1190
00:55:10,443 --> 00:55:12,243
- Did you take your medicine?
- I did.

1191
00:55:13,043 --> 00:55:14,453
I can do the dishes alone.

1192
00:55:14,453 --> 00:55:17,113
No, Ye Ji. There are too many dishes.

1193
00:55:17,453 --> 00:55:18,453
Let's wash them all together and then...

1194
00:55:18,453 --> 00:55:21,223
At least there are fewer dishes than normal.

1195
00:55:22,723 --> 00:55:24,593
Put on an apron. You're wearing white.

1196
00:55:26,784 --> 00:55:28,494
- Do I rinse it?
- Yes, I'll do this instead.

1197
00:55:28,494 --> 00:55:29,524
(Moving)

1198
00:55:29,524 --> 00:55:30,524
I don't need one.

1199
00:55:30,524 --> 00:55:31,564
But you're wearing white.

1200
00:55:31,564 --> 00:55:32,994
- Wear one.
- Okay.

1201
00:55:38,204 --> 00:55:39,934
Do I rinse it, Ye Ji?

1202
00:55:40,774 --> 00:55:41,874
- What?
- Do I rinse it?

1203
00:55:41,874 --> 00:55:42,874
Yes.

1204
00:55:42,874 --> 00:55:44,244
(Ryun Gi helps Ro Bin with an apron.)

1205
00:55:44,244 --> 00:55:45,774
We have great teamwork.

1206
00:55:45,874 --> 00:55:46,874
What?

1207
00:55:50,174 --> 00:55:53,784
(Meanwhile, Do Gon's suyuk is done.)

1208
00:55:53,784 --> 00:55:54,954
Let's eat.

1209
00:55:57,454 --> 00:55:58,784
It's a feast.

1210
00:55:58,784 --> 00:56:00,184
Thank you for the food.

1211
00:56:00,384 --> 00:56:01,924
(Digging in)

1212
00:56:05,394 --> 00:56:06,664
- It tastes good.
- Yes.

1213
00:56:08,534 --> 00:56:11,664
(Satisfied)

1214
00:56:11,964 --> 00:56:13,204
It's really good.

1215
00:56:13,204 --> 00:56:15,704
Right? The meat just melts in your mouth.

1216
00:56:16,934 --> 00:56:18,604
- Is that a scar, Ye Ji?
- Hold on.

1217
00:56:18,604 --> 00:56:20,304
- What?
- Is that a scar?

1218
00:56:20,304 --> 00:56:21,514
Yes, it's the Hickman catheter.

1219
00:56:21,514 --> 00:56:23,144
Your scar is very different from mine.

1220
00:56:23,144 --> 00:56:24,614
- Really?
- Mine looks like this.

1221
00:56:24,714 --> 00:56:26,214
- What?
- Mine's bad, right?

1222
00:56:26,214 --> 00:56:27,314
Here's mine.

1223
00:56:27,414 --> 00:56:29,584
- What are we...
- Matching scars?

1224
00:56:29,814 --> 00:56:31,824
- We have matching scars.
- Right?

1225
00:56:31,824 --> 00:56:33,024
- Mine is...
- What?

1226
00:56:33,554 --> 00:56:34,554
It's big, right?

1227
00:56:35,424 --> 00:56:36,724
Everyone has one.

1228
00:56:37,324 --> 00:56:38,694
- All four of you?
- Mine's here too.

1229
00:56:40,324 --> 00:56:42,364
What? Everyone's the same except me.

1230
00:56:43,564 --> 00:56:44,964
Yours looks really light.

1231
00:56:44,964 --> 00:56:46,204
I put on medicine every day.

1232
00:56:46,604 --> 00:56:48,204
Really, what's with our conversation?

1233
00:56:48,204 --> 00:56:49,274
When it was taken out.

1234
00:56:49,504 --> 00:56:50,534
Interesting.

1235
00:56:51,004 --> 00:56:53,574
- My side hurts.
- Everyone has a mark right here.

1236
00:56:56,174 --> 00:56:57,914
This conversation itself is hilarious.

1237
00:56:59,014 --> 00:57:01,714
- For real.
- "Back in our teens,"

1238
00:57:01,714 --> 00:57:03,384
"didn't we play Super Mario?"

1239
00:57:03,384 --> 00:57:05,454
"Yes, we totally did." That's the vibe I'm getting.

1240
00:57:06,284 --> 00:57:07,454
It sure is funny.

1241
00:57:07,454 --> 00:57:08,654
(It's a shared understanding only we can have.)

1242
00:57:08,654 --> 00:57:09,654
It's totally funny.

1243
00:57:10,964 --> 00:57:12,724
I'm spacing out now that I'm full.

1244
00:57:13,594 --> 00:57:15,564
They'd probably still be out even after a nap.

1245
00:57:16,851 --> 00:57:18,591
- Right.
- The other two.

1246
00:57:20,421 --> 00:57:24,861
(Seon Ho and Na Young haven't come home yet.)

1247
00:57:25,961 --> 00:57:28,701
Seon Ho said proactive words...

1248
00:57:28,801 --> 00:57:31,871
that gave me certainty,

1249
00:57:31,871 --> 00:57:33,371
which was...

1250
00:57:33,371 --> 00:57:37,141
one of the happiest days since moving into the House.

1251
00:57:37,141 --> 00:57:40,851
But he had another date after ours.

1252
00:57:40,851 --> 00:57:42,411
His date seemed like Na Young.

1253
00:57:42,411 --> 00:57:44,551
"What kind of date are they having?"

1254
00:57:44,951 --> 00:57:46,821
It got on my nerves.

1255
00:57:46,921 --> 00:57:49,251
I wanted him to return to the House soon.

1256
00:57:51,091 --> 00:57:53,661
(Gwanghwamun)

1257
00:57:56,561 --> 00:57:59,531
(Na Young is waiting for Seon Ho.)

1258
00:58:00,361 --> 00:58:02,471
(Nervous)

1259
00:58:03,631 --> 00:58:05,641
I was nervous even before the date.

1260
00:58:07,041 --> 00:58:09,311
"We're going on a date. I'll be meeting him soon."

1261
00:58:10,811 --> 00:58:11,911
"How exciting."

1262
00:58:14,681 --> 00:58:16,351
He's constantly on my mind,

1263
00:58:16,351 --> 00:58:17,721
and I'm attracted to him.

1264
00:58:19,421 --> 00:58:20,621
I mean Seon Ho.

1265
00:58:23,121 --> 00:58:27,461
I had this big urge to get to know him more.

1266
00:58:29,391 --> 00:58:34,831
(It's the first date with Seon Ho, whom Na Young was curious about.)

1267
00:58:37,471 --> 00:58:38,871
Here it is.

1268
00:58:38,871 --> 00:58:40,171
- This is bad.
- Here it is.

1269
00:58:40,171 --> 00:58:41,911
Na Young has been waiting a while.

1270
00:58:41,911 --> 00:58:43,771
- She totally did.
- What now?

1271
00:58:43,771 --> 00:58:46,711
What Seon Ho's date with Na Young will be like...

1272
00:58:46,711 --> 00:58:48,051
is critical.

1273
00:58:48,051 --> 00:58:49,651
- It'll be a key point.
- Yes, a key point.

1274
00:58:49,651 --> 00:58:50,981
Oh, no.

1275
00:59:21,411 --> 00:59:23,281
(Na Young spotted Seon Ho.)

1276
00:59:34,361 --> 00:59:36,091
I can't, really.

1277
00:59:40,631 --> 00:59:42,371
Honestly, all I could see was Seon Ho...

1278
00:59:42,371 --> 00:59:44,841
among the crowd.

1279
00:59:47,171 --> 00:59:49,441
My heart was pounding so hard back then.

1280
01:00:03,651 --> 01:00:05,791
I ran into Na Young...

1281
01:00:05,791 --> 01:00:07,891
in front of the traffic lights.

1282
01:00:08,761 --> 01:00:12,731
Maybe because she was wearing an outfit I'd never seen before,

1283
01:00:13,301 --> 01:00:15,031
my heart did flutter a bit.

1284
01:00:16,931 --> 01:00:19,001
(Shocked)

1285
01:00:19,371 --> 01:00:20,601
Hold on a minute.

1286
01:00:20,871 --> 01:00:22,471
- Come on.
- I just...

1287
01:00:22,471 --> 01:00:23,511
Guys.

1288
01:00:23,511 --> 01:00:25,741
- He's not dating Ye Ji yet.
- Right.

1289
01:00:25,741 --> 01:00:27,381
- Guys.
- I forgot.

1290
01:00:27,381 --> 01:00:29,311
Guys, Seon Ho and Ye Ji aren't dating.

1291
01:00:29,311 --> 01:00:30,381
- Right.
- I know,

1292
01:00:30,381 --> 01:00:34,051
but he's never said his heart fluttered for someone before.

1293
01:00:34,051 --> 01:00:35,521
No.

1294
01:00:35,521 --> 01:00:36,691
It's over once your heart flutters.

1295
01:00:36,691 --> 01:00:37,721
Come on, Se Young.

1296
01:00:37,721 --> 01:00:38,921
Calm down.

1297
01:00:39,461 --> 01:00:41,461
- Nothing has started, - She must...

1298
01:00:41,461 --> 01:00:43,491
- but look at how happy she is.
- really like him.

1299
01:00:46,061 --> 01:00:47,771
I can't, really.

1300
01:01:05,921 --> 01:01:08,051
(Embarrassed)

1301
01:01:15,661 --> 01:01:17,231
You're late.

1302
01:01:17,591 --> 01:01:18,731
I'm sorry.

1303
01:01:19,131 --> 01:01:20,231
Aren't you cold?

1304
01:01:20,231 --> 01:01:21,271
Really.

1305
01:01:22,201 --> 01:01:24,201
You're so late.

1306
01:01:25,501 --> 01:01:27,071
You kept me waiting, you know?

1307
01:01:27,071 --> 01:01:28,171
Aren't you cold?

1308
01:01:29,271 --> 01:01:30,971
It's not as cold as expected.

1309
01:01:32,481 --> 01:01:34,311
(Her heart is pounding.)

1310
01:01:37,311 --> 01:01:38,581
Do you know what we're doing today?

1311
01:01:38,581 --> 01:01:39,721
I don't.

1312
01:01:40,851 --> 01:01:42,651
We're going on a bus tour.

1313
01:01:42,651 --> 01:01:43,951
I've never gone on one before.

1314
01:01:43,951 --> 01:01:45,361
It'll take us to Mount Nam.

1315
01:01:45,361 --> 01:01:46,691
- To where?
- Mount Nam.

1316
01:01:46,691 --> 01:01:47,861
The bus goes to Mount Nam?

1317
01:01:47,861 --> 01:01:49,891
- It's a Mount Nam bus tour.
- Nice.

1318
01:01:50,591 --> 01:01:53,031
After the bus tour, we're going to an izakaya to...

1319
01:01:53,261 --> 01:01:54,471
For real?

1320
01:01:55,831 --> 01:01:58,101
- How about it?
- I love it.

1321
01:01:58,101 --> 01:01:59,801
- Okay.
- It'll be our first drink.

1322
01:02:00,201 --> 01:02:01,571
What do you mean by first drink?

1323
01:02:03,041 --> 01:02:04,171
Do we get the tickets here?

1324
01:02:04,171 --> 01:02:05,311
This seems like the place.

1325
01:02:05,311 --> 01:02:06,741
(The date starts with a Mount Nam bus tour.)

1326
01:02:07,281 --> 01:02:08,681
- Hi.
- Hi.

1327
01:02:08,681 --> 01:02:10,511
Hi. For two, please.

1328
01:02:10,511 --> 01:02:11,921
Two for the night view?

1329
01:02:11,921 --> 01:02:13,721
- Yes.
- Okay, two tickets.

1330
01:02:14,851 --> 01:02:16,391
The bus will leave at 7:30pm.

1331
01:02:16,391 --> 01:02:18,461
Boarding will start at 7pm.

1332
01:02:18,461 --> 01:02:20,161
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

1333
01:02:20,161 --> 01:02:21,461
We can get on the bus now.

1334
01:02:21,461 --> 01:02:23,161
Yes, and we'll go on the second floor.

1335
01:02:23,161 --> 01:02:24,261
Really?

1336
01:02:24,531 --> 01:02:25,861
This is a first for me.

1337
01:02:25,861 --> 01:02:27,101
It's that bus.

1338
01:02:31,471 --> 01:02:36,771
(It's their first double-decker bus ride together.)

1339
01:02:39,011 --> 01:02:43,011
(Beneath an open sky)

1340
01:02:43,011 --> 01:02:47,221
(The romance of cruising through Seoul)

1341
01:02:47,821 --> 01:02:49,591
Do you want to sit by the window or the aisle?

1342
01:02:49,591 --> 01:02:51,761
- Wherever you want.
- I want to sit here.

1343
01:02:56,491 --> 01:02:57,661
Aren't you cold?

1344
01:02:58,031 --> 01:03:00,831
I might get a little cold later, but not right now.

1345
01:03:00,931 --> 01:03:02,631
This is very new.

1346
01:03:02,901 --> 01:03:06,141
Had it just been me, I would've never done this.

1347
01:03:06,141 --> 01:03:07,771
Why? How come?

1348
01:03:07,771 --> 01:03:09,811
Going on a bus tour never crossed my mind.

1349
01:03:10,571 --> 01:03:12,741
This is seriously my first time in my life.

1350
01:03:12,741 --> 01:03:13,811
- That's a relief.
- Yes.

1351
01:03:13,811 --> 01:03:15,351
Everything is just so fascinating right now.

1352
01:03:19,721 --> 01:03:21,291
I'm wearing a skirt.

1353
01:03:23,151 --> 01:03:25,361
I did think it was my first time seeing you wear one.

1354
01:03:26,691 --> 01:03:27,691
(Dizzy)

1355
01:03:27,691 --> 01:03:29,191
Oh, my gosh.

1356
01:03:29,191 --> 01:03:30,791
- An appeal.
- An appeal.

1357
01:03:30,791 --> 01:03:32,161
- "I came dressed up." - "I feel shy."

1358
01:03:32,161 --> 01:03:33,831
- "I'm feeling shy." - "I dressed up for you."

1359
01:03:33,831 --> 01:03:35,501
"I dressed up, so what?"

1360
01:03:35,501 --> 01:03:37,871
It seems like Seon Ho's heart fluttered a little.

1361
01:03:39,071 --> 01:03:40,401
It shouldn't have.

1362
01:03:40,401 --> 01:03:42,011
Why open your eyes like that?

1363
01:03:43,341 --> 01:03:44,471
You took me by surprise.

1364
01:03:44,471 --> 01:03:45,481
(Her inner thoughts keep slipping out.)

1365
01:03:45,881 --> 01:03:47,241
(Embarrassed)

1366
01:03:48,751 --> 01:03:50,311
So? I look different, right?

1367
01:03:50,311 --> 01:03:52,421
Really, it's a twist. But the skirt looks good.

1368
01:03:52,421 --> 01:03:53,781
- Really?
- It really does look good on you.

1369
01:03:54,321 --> 01:03:55,491
I suddenly feel...

1370
01:04:00,591 --> 01:04:01,591
(Glancing)

1371
01:04:02,631 --> 01:04:03,931
(Glancing)

1372
01:04:05,401 --> 01:04:06,901
(Nervous)

1373
01:04:08,901 --> 01:04:10,301
Did you have no idea?

1374
01:04:10,801 --> 01:04:11,871
That I was curious about you?

1375
01:04:11,871 --> 01:04:13,271
No, because...

1376
01:04:15,511 --> 01:04:18,241
First off, our personalities are the complete opposite.

1377
01:04:18,481 --> 01:04:20,781
I jumped the gun right away and thought,

1378
01:04:20,781 --> 01:04:22,111
"I doubt she's interested in me."

1379
01:04:22,111 --> 01:04:23,151
That's not true.

1380
01:04:23,451 --> 01:04:24,651
Is that so?

1381
01:04:25,481 --> 01:04:26,921
You were my choice since Day One.

1382
01:04:26,921 --> 01:04:29,091
(You were my choice since Day One.)

1383
01:04:29,091 --> 01:04:32,091
I thought you had zero interest in me.

1384
01:04:32,091 --> 01:04:34,221
No, I really...

1385
01:04:34,221 --> 01:04:36,691
I have brought your name up ever since my first interview.

1386
01:04:37,091 --> 01:04:38,101
(Surprised)

1387
01:04:38,301 --> 01:04:40,701
Really, Na Young opens up...

1388
01:04:40,701 --> 01:04:41,771
- about everything.
- Right?

1389
01:04:41,771 --> 01:04:44,401
Ye Ji and Na Young are different, right?

1390
01:04:44,401 --> 01:04:46,701
- Na Young is very honest.
- Straightforward.

1391
01:04:46,701 --> 01:04:48,341
Meanwhile, Ye Ji is...

1392
01:04:48,341 --> 01:04:50,771
She's not completely straightforward and frank.

1393
01:04:50,771 --> 01:04:52,681
- Ye Ji is quite shy.
- Yes.

1394
01:04:52,681 --> 01:04:54,881
Seon Ho said his heart fluttered earlier.

1395
01:04:55,281 --> 01:04:57,151
I think I like guys...

1396
01:04:57,151 --> 01:05:00,021
who are the opposite of me.

1397
01:05:01,651 --> 01:05:02,991
I had no idea.

1398
01:05:04,591 --> 01:05:07,391
I can't remember it clearly.

1399
01:05:08,291 --> 01:05:09,791
Did you say you don't mind older girls?

1400
01:05:09,791 --> 01:05:11,501
- You see...
- What did you...

1401
01:05:11,501 --> 01:05:14,261
Honestly, I don't mind the age as long as I like her.

1402
01:05:14,671 --> 01:05:17,501
But when I date someone I like,

1403
01:05:18,398 --> 01:05:20,998
there are times I think about our far future.

1404
01:05:21,628 --> 01:05:24,398
Older girls have an optimal average age...

1405
01:05:24,398 --> 01:05:26,168
for marriage, right?

1406
01:05:26,168 --> 01:05:29,908
If I can understand and respect that,

1407
01:05:29,908 --> 01:05:31,438
age doesn't matter.

1408
01:05:31,438 --> 01:05:35,078
I'm sure it's different for everyone.

1409
01:05:35,078 --> 01:05:37,608
In my case, I don't plan...

1410
01:05:38,718 --> 01:05:40,018
on getting married fast.

1411
01:05:40,848 --> 01:05:42,518
I'm not saying this to fancy you.

1412
01:05:42,518 --> 01:05:43,618
It has always been the case.

1413
01:05:43,618 --> 01:05:45,618
I get it.

1414
01:05:46,318 --> 01:05:49,058
I didn't want you to think it that way.

1415
01:05:49,058 --> 01:05:50,228
But really.

1416
01:05:50,228 --> 01:05:52,058
(Thinking)

1417
01:05:52,528 --> 01:05:53,758
In short, you don't care?

1418
01:05:53,758 --> 01:05:56,468
No, I don't, as long as I have feelings for her.

1419
01:05:58,098 --> 01:06:01,098
(She heard a satisfying answer.)

1420
01:06:04,108 --> 01:06:05,678
- We're off.
- Yes.

1421
01:06:09,708 --> 01:06:11,678
This is my first time ever.

1422
01:06:11,678 --> 01:06:13,478
- It's already fun.
- Same here.

1423
01:06:15,488 --> 01:06:17,718
I haven't been to Mount Nam in ages.

1424
01:06:18,088 --> 01:06:20,988
This will be my first time going to Mount Nam in my life.

1425
01:06:21,588 --> 01:06:23,928
But it's a must-do for dates.

1426
01:06:23,928 --> 01:06:25,928
Since I live in the provinces,

1427
01:06:25,928 --> 01:06:28,628
I'm like, "Must we really travel to Seoul for a date?"

1428
01:06:33,368 --> 01:06:37,638
(A moment of sharing each other's firsts)

1429
01:06:39,578 --> 01:06:40,778
(Rustling)

1430
01:06:40,778 --> 01:06:41,948
- Oh, dear.
- My gosh.

1431
01:06:44,878 --> 01:06:49,088
(Branches brush past, almost close enough to touch.)

1432
01:06:52,018 --> 01:06:54,018
The trees are so low here.

1433
01:06:57,228 --> 01:06:58,598
(Stunned)

1434
01:06:59,598 --> 01:07:00,858
Interesting.

1435
01:07:03,428 --> 01:07:07,538
(As they ride on for a while)

1436
01:07:07,698 --> 01:07:09,468
It's so pretty. Look.

1437
01:07:09,568 --> 01:07:10,838
(Surprised)

1438
01:07:13,938 --> 01:07:15,378
It's really pretty.

1439
01:07:16,808 --> 01:07:19,448
It's such a beautiful time right now.

1440
01:07:22,918 --> 01:07:24,418
(They slowly draw closer to the glowing red sunset.)

1441
01:07:24,418 --> 01:07:26,858
- We were too focused on talking.
- We didn't look around.

1442
01:07:26,858 --> 01:07:28,758
Isn't it beautiful right now?

1443
01:07:31,288 --> 01:07:33,458
Photos... Should I take one with this?

1444
01:07:35,928 --> 01:07:37,228
It sure is pretty.

1445
01:07:45,838 --> 01:07:47,278
Really, how beautiful.

1446
01:07:49,508 --> 01:07:51,178
The sunset can be seen over there.

1447
01:07:51,178 --> 01:07:52,318
Right.

1448
01:07:54,278 --> 01:07:55,548
It's beautiful over there.

1449
01:07:57,688 --> 01:08:01,688
(A view that makes you watch without saying a word)

1450
01:08:07,658 --> 01:08:09,568
I move around Seoul so often.

1451
01:08:09,568 --> 01:08:10,728
Why does it feel so different?

1452
01:08:10,928 --> 01:08:12,668
"This is why people come."

1453
01:08:12,668 --> 01:08:14,768
I'm suddenly getting this thought.

1454
01:08:15,038 --> 01:08:16,208
- Right?
- Yes.

1455
01:08:16,338 --> 01:08:17,338
It feels different.

1456
01:08:17,338 --> 01:08:20,238
I move around here often because of work.

1457
01:08:22,608 --> 01:08:24,208
But I never thought...

1458
01:08:25,148 --> 01:08:27,218
it was this pretty because I came here all the time.

1459
01:08:27,218 --> 01:08:28,318
You know what I mean, right?

1460
01:08:32,458 --> 01:08:33,988
(Peeking)

1461
01:08:49,638 --> 01:08:51,008
We're not going to catch colds, are we?

1462
01:08:52,678 --> 01:08:56,048
Even if we do, I think it will be worth it.

1463
01:08:56,048 --> 01:08:58,418
(Even if we do, I think it will be worth it.)

1464
01:09:00,878 --> 01:09:02,548
- But...
- The wind is...

1465
01:09:02,548 --> 01:09:04,348
(Her hair is blowing in the wind.)

1466
01:09:06,558 --> 01:09:07,618
My hair!

1467
01:09:15,928 --> 01:09:17,498
The wind was too strong,

1468
01:09:18,738 --> 01:09:20,668
and our hair was flying all over the place.

1469
01:09:24,038 --> 01:09:26,738
I thought it was like a scene from a movie poster.

1470
01:09:26,738 --> 01:09:28,148
(I thought it was like a scene from a movie poster.)

1471
01:09:29,078 --> 01:09:30,278
Gosh!

1472
01:09:30,608 --> 01:09:32,278
My gosh. It's too romantic.

1473
01:09:32,678 --> 01:09:34,548
- It's such a nice picture.
- Right.

1474
01:09:34,548 --> 01:09:36,588
- The two look so good together.
- Right.

1475
01:09:36,588 --> 01:09:39,488
I think it's possible for them to fall in love...

1476
01:09:39,488 --> 01:09:40,658
- in this situation.
- It's so romantic.

1477
01:09:40,658 --> 01:09:42,058
Right. It's so romantic.

1478
01:09:42,388 --> 01:09:44,658
Aren't those the eyes of the ones fallen in love?

1479
01:09:44,658 --> 01:09:46,858
Gosh! My heart is starting to break.

1480
01:09:47,228 --> 01:09:48,768
I don't know what to do!

1481
01:09:48,768 --> 01:09:50,898
This feels strange for some reason.

1482
01:09:50,898 --> 01:09:53,838
Why am I feeling this way?

1483
01:09:53,938 --> 01:09:55,068
I feel dizzy.

1484
01:09:55,868 --> 01:09:57,508
- You feel dizzy?
- I feel dizzy.

1485
01:09:57,508 --> 01:09:58,978
I don't know what to do.

1486
01:09:58,978 --> 01:10:00,308
You should keep your eyes closed for five minutes.

1487
01:10:01,038 --> 01:10:03,278
- Go and take five minutes off.
- Oh, no!

1488
01:10:08,048 --> 01:10:09,448
Our hair was flying around in the wind,

1489
01:10:09,448 --> 01:10:11,018
and we met each other's eyes.

1490
01:10:11,388 --> 01:10:14,718
Being with him like that felt exciting.

1491
01:10:16,058 --> 01:10:19,558
It was going to become a memorable moment.

1492
01:10:21,528 --> 01:10:22,528
(Gazing)

1493
01:10:22,728 --> 01:10:23,728
(Turning)

1494
01:10:25,238 --> 01:10:27,068
I can't see myself.

1495
01:10:28,060 --> 01:10:29,900
- Do I look okay?
- You look fine.

1496
01:10:29,900 --> 01:10:31,270
I think my hair is the problem.

1497
01:10:42,010 --> 01:10:45,750
(Meanwhile, Ye Ji waits for Seon Ho.)

1498
01:10:50,086 --> 01:10:54,326
(She checks the time.)

1499
01:10:54,776 --> 01:10:56,606
(Letting out a sigh)

1500
01:11:03,186 --> 01:11:08,956
(She feels bothered about Seon Ho not coming back.)

1501
01:11:27,976 --> 01:11:29,076
It's starting to come up.

1502
01:11:29,106 --> 01:11:30,716
I'll apologize instead.

1503
01:11:33,546 --> 01:11:35,216
- Ye Ji looks angry.
- Look at her.

1504
01:11:35,216 --> 01:11:36,916
She's wondering why he still isn't back.

1505
01:11:37,635 --> 01:11:39,295
I think she will feel quite upset.

1506
01:11:39,565 --> 01:11:42,065
She enjoyed a dreamlike date with him.

1507
01:11:42,065 --> 01:11:44,635
Now, she has to wait for 3 to 4 hours...

1508
01:11:44,635 --> 01:11:46,405
for him to come back from a date with another woman.

1509
01:11:48,405 --> 01:11:50,815
- This is killing me.
- She's checking the time.

1510
01:11:56,695 --> 01:11:58,088
What do I do?

1511
01:12:04,071 --> 01:12:06,371
(Sighing)

1512
01:12:10,881 --> 01:12:18,581
(She tries to suppress her anxiety.)

1513
01:12:25,861 --> 01:12:26,861
Well...

1514
01:12:26,861 --> 01:12:27,861
(At that time)

1515
01:12:30,530 --> 01:12:31,700
- This is exciting.
- Right.

1516
01:12:31,700 --> 01:12:32,730
It's beyond my expectations.

1517
01:12:35,800 --> 01:12:38,300
Didn't you say you wanted to meet a younger guy?

1518
01:12:38,300 --> 01:12:40,200
- What?
- You wanted to meet a younger guy.

1519
01:12:40,200 --> 01:12:41,570
It's because I've never met someone younger.

1520
01:12:41,770 --> 01:12:44,540
Well, my younger brother was born in 1996.

1521
01:12:45,410 --> 01:12:46,540
He's much older than me.

1522
01:12:46,540 --> 01:12:48,010
(Born in 1999)

1523
01:12:48,010 --> 01:12:50,540
That was why it felt quite awkward.

1524
01:12:50,540 --> 01:12:51,550
Right.

1525
01:12:52,050 --> 01:12:53,580
Whenever...

1526
01:12:54,219 --> 01:12:55,859
guys call me "nuna,"

1527
01:12:56,319 --> 01:12:59,159
they feel like younger brothers to me.

1528
01:13:00,429 --> 01:13:03,699
Or it can be cuter instead.

1529
01:13:04,059 --> 01:13:05,769
- The way you're called nuna?
- Right.

1530
01:13:05,769 --> 01:13:07,329
- How?
- I don't know.

1531
01:13:07,329 --> 01:13:09,399
- "Nunang?" - No. That's not what I meant.

1532
01:13:10,069 --> 01:13:11,369
- That's not what I meant.
- How?

1533
01:13:11,369 --> 01:13:14,409
Well, how should I put it?

1534
01:13:15,409 --> 01:13:18,779
After hearing this, if you called me by my name,

1535
01:13:18,779 --> 01:13:20,849
it would've really made my heart flutter.

1536
01:13:20,849 --> 01:13:22,879
(It would've really made my heart flutter.)

1537
01:13:23,119 --> 01:13:25,889
It's hard for you to drop the honorifics, right?

1538
01:13:26,089 --> 01:13:27,659
- Yes.
- I see.

1539
01:13:28,719 --> 01:13:31,029
I don't wish to force you to do anything.

1540
01:13:31,329 --> 01:13:32,829
I wish for you to do whatever you're comfortable with.

1541
01:13:32,829 --> 01:13:34,059
(Na Young matches Seon Ho's pace.)

1542
01:13:34,729 --> 01:13:38,229
(N Seoul Tower can be seen from afar.)

1543
01:13:39,069 --> 01:13:40,569
Mount Nam can be seen now.

1544
01:13:41,234 --> 01:13:42,464
It's so pretty.

1545
01:13:52,674 --> 01:13:57,754
(They arrive at the Mount Nam bus stop past the Han River.)

1546
01:14:00,388 --> 01:14:01,398
It's so pretty.

1547
01:14:01,398 --> 01:14:03,228
From what I remember,

1548
01:14:03,228 --> 01:14:05,268
the night view was amazing from that side.

1549
01:14:05,268 --> 01:14:06,468
There's a good spot?

1550
01:14:08,760 --> 01:14:09,760
(Amazed)

1551
01:14:09,760 --> 01:14:11,230
It's much bigger than you think, isn't it?

1552
01:14:11,400 --> 01:14:13,970
It looks different from how it looked from afar.

1553
01:14:13,970 --> 01:14:15,500
Right.

1554
01:14:22,947 --> 01:14:24,317
We should get warm drinks.

1555
01:14:24,317 --> 01:14:25,447
- Should we do that?
- Yes.

1556
01:14:31,317 --> 01:14:34,057
- We should carry them...
- Should we walk around?

1557
01:14:34,057 --> 01:14:35,987
and move up the Sky Forest Trail.

1558
01:14:36,627 --> 01:14:38,757
- What would you like?
- Americano.

1559
01:14:39,557 --> 01:14:40,897
- Iced?
- No.

1560
01:14:40,897 --> 01:14:41,967
Right.

1561
01:14:42,727 --> 01:14:44,067
I want the same.

1562
01:14:44,937 --> 01:14:46,337
You drink coffee?

1563
01:14:46,597 --> 01:14:48,067
Yes. I like coffee.

1564
01:14:54,107 --> 01:14:56,077
Why don't you speak with an accent?

1565
01:14:56,277 --> 01:14:57,377
I don't speak with an accent?

1566
01:14:57,377 --> 01:14:58,747
People said I spoke with an accent often.

